INSERT INTO `bills` VALUES
(74670,'hb1322',30,'house','Certified registered nurse anesthetist; elimination of supervision requirement.',87,'<b>Certified registered nurse anesthetist; elimination of supervision requirement.</b> Eliminates the requirement that certified registered nurse anesthetists practice under the supervision of a doctor of medicine, osteopathy, podiatry, or dentistry. The bill provides that certified registered nurse anesthetists shall practice in consultation with a doctor of medicine, osteopathy, podiatry, or dentistry and in accordance with regulations jointly promulgated by the Board of Medicine and the Board of Nursing.','<br><center><b>HOUSE BILL NO. 1322</b></center>\r \r <center>AMENDMENT IN THE NATURE OF A SUBSTITUTE</center>\r \r <center>(Proposed by the House Committee on Health and Human Services</center>\r \r <center>on February 8, 2024)</center>\r \r <center>(Patron Prior to Substitute--Delegate Sickles)</center>\r \r <i>A BILL to amend and reenact §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a> of the\r Code of Virginia, relating to certified registered nurse anesthetist;\r elimination of supervision requirement.</i>\r \r <p>Be it enacted by the General Assembly of Virginia:</p>\r \r <p>1. That §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a> of the Code of Virginia\r are amended and reenacted as follows:</p>\r \r <p>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a>. Definitions.</p>\r \r <p>As used in this chapter, unless the context requires a\r different meaning:</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Acupuncturist&quot; means an individual approved by the\r Board to practice acupuncture. This is limited to &quot;licensed\r acupuncturist&quot; which means an individual other than a doctor of medicine,\r osteopathy, chiropractic or podiatry who has successfully completed the\r requirements for licensure established by the Board (approved titles are\r limited to: Licensed Acupuncturist, Lic.Ac., and L.Ac.).</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Advanced practice registered nurse&quot; means a\r certified nurse midwife, certified registered nurse anesthetist, clinical nurse\r specialist, or nurse practitioner who is jointly licensed by the Boards of\r Medicine and Nursing pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>, has completed an advanced graduate-level\r education program in a specialty category of nursing, and has passed a national\r certifying examination for that specialty.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Auricular acupuncture&quot; means the subcutaneous\r insertion of sterile, disposable acupuncture needles in predetermined, bilateral\r locations in the outer ear when used exclusively and specifically in the\r context of a chemical dependency treatment program.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Birth control&quot; means contraceptive methods that are\r approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. &quot;Birth control&quot;\r shall not be considered abortion for the purposes of Title 18.2.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Board&quot; means the Board of Medicine.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Certified nurse midwife&quot; means an advanced practice\r registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of nurse midwifery and who\r is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as an advanced\r practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Certified registered nurse anesthetist&quot; means an\r advanced practice registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of nurse\r anesthesia, who is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as an\r advanced practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>, and who practices<s>\r under the supervision of</s><ins> in consultation with</ins> a doctor of medicine,\r osteopathy, podiatry, or dentistry but is not subject to the practice agreement\r requirement described in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Clinical nurse specialist&quot; means an advanced\r practice registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of clinical nurse\r specialist and who is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as\r an advanced practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Collaboration&quot; means the communication and\r decision-making process among health care providers who are members of a\r patient care team related to the treatment of a patient that includes the\r degree of cooperation necessary to provide treatment and care of the patient\r and includes (i) communication of data and information about the treatment and\r care of a patient, including the exchange of clinical observations and\r assessments, and (ii) development of an appropriate plan of care, including\r decisions regarding the health care provided, accessing and assessment of\r appropriate additional resources or expertise, and arrangement of appropriate\r referrals, testing, or studies.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Consultation&quot; means communicating data and\r information, exchanging clinical observations and assessments, accessing and\r assessing additional resources and expertise, problem-solving, and arranging\r for referrals, testing, or studies.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Genetic counselor&quot; means a person licensed by the\r Board to engage in the practice of genetic counseling.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Healing arts&quot; means the arts and sciences dealing\r with the prevention, diagnosis, treatment and cure or alleviation of human\r physical or mental ailments, conditions, diseases, pain or infirmities.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Licensed certified midwife&quot; means a person who is\r licensed as a certified midwife by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Medical malpractice judgment&quot; means any final order\r of any court entering judgment against a licensee of the Board that arises out of\r any tort action or breach of contract action for personal injuries or wrongful\r death, based on health care or professional services rendered, or that should\r have been rendered, by a health care provider, to a patient.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Medical malpractice settlement&quot; means any written\r agreement and release entered into by or on behalf of a licensee of the Board\r in response to a written claim for money damages that arises out of any\r personal injuries or wrongful death, based on health care or professional\r services rendered, or that should have been rendered, by a health care\r provider, to a patient.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Nurse practitioner&quot; means an advanced practice\r registered nurse, other than an advanced practice registered nurse licensed by\r the Boards of Medicine and Nursing in the category of certified nurse midwife,\r certified registered nurse anesthetist, or clinical nurse specialist, who is\r jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Occupational therapy assistant&quot; means an individual\r who has met the requirements of the Board for licensure and who works under the\r supervision of a licensed occupational therapist to assist in the practice of\r occupational therapy.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Patient care team&quot; means a multidisciplinary team\r of health care providers actively functioning as a unit with the management and\r leadership of one or more patient care team physicians for the purpose of\r providing and delivering health care to a patient or group of patients.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Patient care team physician&quot; means a physician who\r is actively licensed to practice medicine in the Commonwealth, who regularly\r practices medicine in the Commonwealth, and who provides management and\r leadership in the care of patients as part of a patient care team.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Patient care team podiatrist&quot; means a podiatrist\r who is actively licensed to practice podiatry in the Commonwealth, who\r regularly practices podiatry in the Commonwealth, and who provides management\r and leadership in the care of patients as part of a patient care team.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Physician assistant&quot; means a health care\r professional who has met the requirements of the Board for licensure as a\r physician assistant.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of acupuncture&quot; means the stimulation of\r certain points on or near the surface of the body by the insertion of needles to\r prevent or modify the perception of pain or to normalize physiological\r functions, including pain control, for the treatment of certain ailments or\r conditions of the body and includes the techniques of electroacupuncture,\r cupping and moxibustion. The practice of acupuncture does not include the use\r of physical therapy, chiropractic, or osteopathic manipulative techniques; the\r use or prescribing of any drugs, medications, serums or vaccines; or the\r procedure of auricular acupuncture as exempted in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a> when used in the\r context of a chemical dependency treatment program for patients eligible for\r federal, state or local public funds by an employee of the program who is\r trained and approved by the National Acupuncture Detoxification Association or\r an equivalent certifying body.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of athletic training&quot; means the\r prevention, recognition, evaluation, and treatment of injuries or conditions\r related to athletic or recreational activity that requires physical skill and\r utilizes strength, power, endurance, speed, flexibility, range of motion or\r agility or a substantially similar injury or condition resulting from\r occupational activity immediately upon the onset of such injury or condition;\r and subsequent treatment and rehabilitation of such injuries or conditions\r under the direction of the patient\'s physician or under the direction of any\r doctor of medicine, osteopathy, chiropractic, podiatry, or dentistry, while\r using heat, light, sound, cold, electricity, exercise or mechanical or other\r devices.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of behavior analysis&quot; means the design,\r implementation, and evaluation of environmental modifications, using behavioral\r stimuli and consequences, to produce socially significant improvement in human\r behavior, including the use of direct observation, measurement, and functional\r analysis of the relationship between environment and behavior.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of chiropractic&quot; means the adjustment of\r the 24 movable vertebrae of the spinal column, and assisting nature for the\r purpose of normalizing the transmission of nerve energy, but does not include\r the use of surgery, obstetrics, osteopathy, or the administration or\r prescribing of any drugs, medicines, serums, or vaccines. &quot;Practice of\r chiropractic&quot; shall include (i) requesting, receiving, and reviewing a\r patient\'s medical and physical history, including information related to past\r surgical and nonsurgical treatment of the patient and controlled substances\r prescribed to the patient, and (ii) documenting in a patient\'s record\r information related to the condition and symptoms of the patient, the\r examination and evaluation of the patient made by the doctor of chiropractic,\r and treatment provided to the patient by the doctor of chiropractic.\r &quot;Practice of chiropractic&quot; shall also include performing the physical\r examination of an applicant for a commercial driver\'s license or commercial\r learner\'s permit pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/46.2-341.12\">46.2-341.12</a> if the practitioner has (i) applied\r for and received certification as a medical examiner pursuant to 49 C.F.R. Part\r 390, Subpart D and (ii) registered with the National Registry of Certified\r Medical Examiners.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of genetic counseling&quot; means (i) obtaining\r and evaluating individual and family medical histories to assess the risk of\r genetic medical conditions and diseases in a patient, his offspring, and other\r family members; (ii) discussing the features, history, diagnosis, environmental\r factors, and risk management of genetic medical conditions and diseases; (iii)\r ordering genetic laboratory tests and other diagnostic studies necessary for genetic\r assessment; (iv) integrating the results with personal and family medical\r history to assess and communicate risk factors for genetic medical conditions\r and diseases; (v) evaluating the patient\'s and family\'s responses to the\r medical condition or risk of recurrence and providing client-centered\r counseling and anticipatory guidance; (vi) identifying and utilizing community\r resources that provide medical, educational, financial, and psychosocial\r support and advocacy; and (vii) providing written documentation of medical,\r genetic, and counseling information for families and health care professionals.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of licensed certified midwifery&quot; means the\r provision of primary health care for preadolescents, adolescents, and adults\r within the scope of practice of a certified midwife established in accordance\r with the Standards for the Practice of Midwifery set by the American College of\r Nurse-Midwives, including (i) providing sexual and reproductive care and care\r during pregnancy and childbirth, postpartum care, and care for the newborn for\r up to 28 days following the birth of the child; (ii) prescribing of\r pharmacological and non-pharmacological therapies within the scope of the\r practice of midwifery; (iii) consulting or collaborating with or referring\r patients to such other health care providers as may be appropriate for the care\r of the patients; and (iv) serving as an educator in the theory and practice of\r midwifery.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of medicine or osteopathic medicine&quot; means\r the prevention, diagnosis, and treatment of human physical or mental ailments,\r conditions, diseases, pain, or infirmities by any means or method.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of occupational therapy&quot; means the\r therapeutic use of occupations for habilitation and rehabilitation to enhance\r physical health, mental health, and cognitive functioning and includes the\r evaluation, analysis, assessment, and delivery of education and training in\r basic and instrumental activities of daily living; the design, fabrication, and\r application of orthoses (splints); the design, selection, and use of adaptive\r equipment and assistive technologies; therapeutic activities to enhance\r functional performance; vocational evaluation and training; and consultation\r concerning the adaptation of physical, sensory, and social environments.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of podiatry&quot; means the prevention,\r diagnosis, treatment, and cure or alleviation of physical conditions, diseases,\r pain, or infirmities of the human foot and ankle, including the medical,\r mechanical and surgical treatment of the ailments of the human foot and ankle,\r but does not include amputation of the foot proximal to the transmetatarsal\r level through the metatarsal shafts. Amputations proximal to the\r metatarsal-phalangeal joints may only be performed in a hospital or ambulatory\r surgery facility accredited by an organization listed in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2939\">54.1-2939</a>. The\r practice includes the diagnosis and treatment of lower extremity ulcers;\r however, the treatment of severe lower extremity ulcers proximal to the foot\r and ankle may only be performed by appropriately trained, credentialed\r podiatrists in an approved hospital or ambulatory surgery center at which the\r podiatrist has privileges, as described in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2939\">54.1-2939</a>. The Board of Medicine\r shall determine whether a specific type of treatment of the foot and ankle is\r within the scope of practice of podiatry.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of radiologic technology&quot; means the\r application of ionizing radiation to human beings for diagnostic or therapeutic\r purposes.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of respiratory care&quot; means the (i)\r administration of pharmacological, diagnostic, and therapeutic agents related\r to respiratory care procedures necessary to implement a treatment, disease\r prevention, pulmonary rehabilitative, or diagnostic regimen prescribed by a\r practitioner of medicine or osteopathic medicine; (ii) transcription and\r implementation of the written or verbal orders of a practitioner of medicine or\r osteopathic medicine pertaining to the practice of respiratory care; (iii)\r observation and monitoring of signs and symptoms, general behavior, general\r physical response to respiratory care treatment and diagnostic testing,\r including determination of whether such signs, symptoms, reactions, behavior or\r general physical response exhibit abnormal characteristics; and (iv)\r implementation of respiratory care procedures, based on observed abnormalities,\r or appropriate reporting, referral, respiratory care protocols or changes in\r treatment pursuant to the written or verbal orders by a licensed practitioner\r of medicine or osteopathic medicine or the initiation of emergency procedures,\r pursuant to the Board\'s regulations or as otherwise authorized by law. The\r practice of respiratory care may be performed in any clinic, hospital, skilled\r nursing facility, private dwelling or other place deemed appropriate by the\r Board in accordance with the written or verbal order of a practitioner of\r medicine or osteopathic medicine, and shall be performed under qualified\r medical direction.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of surgical assisting&quot; means the\r performance of significant surgical tasks, including manipulation of organs,\r suturing of tissue, placement of hemostatic agents, injection of local\r anesthetic, harvesting of veins, implementation of devices, and other duties as\r directed by a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, or podiatry under the\r direct supervision of a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, or podiatry.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Qualified medical direction&quot; means, in the context\r of the practice of respiratory care, having readily accessible to the\r respiratory therapist a licensed practitioner of medicine or osteopathic medicine\r who has specialty training or experience in the management of acute and chronic\r respiratory disorders and who is responsible for the quality, safety, and\r appropriateness of the respiratory services provided by the respiratory\r therapist.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Radiologic technologist&quot; means an individual, other\r than a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, podiatry, or chiropractic or a\r dentist licensed pursuant to Chapter 27 (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2700\">54.1-2700</a> et seq.), who (i)\r performs, may be called upon to perform, or is licensed to perform a comprehensive\r scope of diagnostic or therapeutic radiologic procedures employing ionizing\r radiation and (ii) is delegated or exercises responsibility for the operation\r of radiation-generating equipment, the shielding of patient and staff from\r unnecessary radiation, the appropriate exposure of radiographs, the\r administration of radioactive chemical compounds under the direction of an\r authorized user as specified by regulations of the Department of Health, or\r other procedures that contribute to any significant extent to the site or\r dosage of ionizing radiation to which a patient is exposed.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Radiologic technologist, limited&quot; means an\r individual, other than a licensed radiologic technologist, dental hygienist, or\r person who is otherwise authorized by the Board of Dentistry under Chapter 27\r (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2700\">54.1-2700</a> et seq.) and the regulations pursuant thereto, who performs\r diagnostic radiographic procedures employing equipment that emits ionizing\r radiation that is limited to specific areas of the human body.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Radiologist assistant&quot; means an individual who has\r met the requirements of the Board for licensure as an advanced-level radiologic\r technologist and who, under the direct supervision of a licensed doctor of\r medicine or osteopathy specializing in the field of radiology, is authorized to\r (i) assess and evaluate the physiological and psychological responsiveness of\r patients undergoing radiologic procedures; (ii) evaluate image quality, make\r initial observations, and communicate observations to the supervising\r radiologist; (iii) administer contrast media or other medications prescribed by\r the supervising radiologist; and (iv) perform, or assist the supervising\r radiologist to perform, any other procedure consistent with the guidelines\r adopted by the American College of Radiology, the American Society of\r Radiologic Technologists, and the American Registry of Radiologic\r Technologists.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Respiratory care&quot; means the practice of the allied\r health profession responsible for the direct and indirect services, including\r inhalation therapy and respiratory therapy, in the treatment, management,\r diagnostic testing, control, and care of patients with deficiencies and\r abnormalities associated with the cardiopulmonary system under qualified\r medical direction.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Surgical assistant&quot; means an individual who has met\r the requirements of the Board for licensure as a surgical assistant and who\r works under the direct supervision of a licensed doctor of medicine,\r osteopathy, or podiatry.</p>\r \r <p>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>. Licensure and practice of advanced practice\r registered nurses.</p>\r \r <p>A. As used in this section, &quot;clinical experience&quot;\r means the postgraduate delivery of health care directly to patients pursuant to\r a practice agreement with a patient care team physician.</p>\r \r <p>B. The Board of Medicine and the Board of Nursing shall jointly\r prescribe the regulations governing the licensure of advanced practice\r registered nurses. It is unlawful for a person to practice as an advanced\r practice registered nurse in the Commonwealth unless he holds such a joint\r license.</p>\r \r <p>C. Every nurse practitioner who meets the requirements of\r subsection I shall maintain appropriate collaboration and consultation, as\r evidenced in a written or electronic practice agreement, with at least one\r patient care team physician. A nurse practitioner who meets the requirements of\r subsection I may practice without a written or electronic practice agreement. A\r certified nurse midwife shall practice pursuant to subsection H. A clinical\r nurse specialist shall practice pursuant to subsection J. A certified\r registered nurse anesthetist shall practice<s> under the supervision of</s><ins>\r in consultation with</ins> a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, podiatry,\r or dentistry<ins> and under the regulations jointly promulgated by the Board of\r Medicine and the Board of Nursing</ins>. An advanced practice registered nurse\r who is appointed as a medical examiner pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-282\">32.1-282</a> shall practice in\r collaboration with a licensed doctor of medicine or osteopathic medicine who\r has been appointed to serve as a medical examiner pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-282\">32.1-282</a>.\r Collaboration and consultation among advanced practice registered nurses and\r patient care team physicians may be provided through telemedicine as described\r in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/38.2-3418.16\">38.2-3418.16</a>.</p>\r \r <p>Physicians on patient care teams may require that an advanced practice\r registered nurse be covered by a professional liability insurance policy with\r limits equal to the current limitation on damages set forth in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/8.01-581.15\">8.01-581.15</a>.</p>\r \r <p>Service on a patient care team by a patient care team member\r shall not, by the existence of such service alone, establish or create\r liability for the actions or inactions of other team members.</p>\r \r <p>D. The Boards of Medicine and Nursing shall jointly promulgate\r regulations specifying collaboration and consultation among physicians and\r advanced practice registered nurses working as part of patient care teams that\r shall include the development of, and periodic review and revision of, a\r written or electronic practice agreement; guidelines for availability and\r ongoing communications that define consultation among the collaborating parties\r and the patient; and periodic joint evaluation of the services delivered.\r Practice agreements shall include provisions for (i) periodic review of health\r records, which may include visits to the site where health care is delivered,\r in the manner and at the frequency determined by the advanced practice\r registered nurse and the patient care team physician and (ii) input from\r appropriate health care providers in complex clinical cases and patient\r emergencies and for referrals. Evidence of a practice agreement shall be\r maintained by an advanced practice registered nurse and provided to the Boards\r upon request. For advanced practice registered nurses providing care to\r patients within a hospital or health care system, the practice agreement may be\r included as part of documents delineating the advanced practice registered\r nurse\'s clinical privileges or the electronic or written delineation of duties\r and responsibilities in collaboration and consultation with a patient care team\r physician.</p>\r \r <p>E. The Boards of Medicine and Nursing may issue a license by\r endorsement to an applicant to practice as an advanced practice registered\r nurse if the applicant has been licensed as an advanced practice registered\r nurse under the laws of another state and, pursuant to regulations of the\r Boards, the applicant meets the qualifications for licensure required of\r advanced practice registered nurses in the Commonwealth. An advanced practice\r registered nurse to whom a license is issued by endorsement may practice\r without a practice agreement with a patient care team physician pursuant to\r subsection I if such application provides an attestation to the Boards that the\r applicant has completed the equivalent of at least five years of full-time\r clinical experience, as determined by the Boards, in accordance with the laws\r of the state in which the nurse practitioner was licensed.</p>\r \r <p>F. Pending the outcome of the next National Specialty\r Examination, the Boards may jointly grant temporary licensure to advanced\r practice registered nurses.</p>\r \r <p>G. In the event a physician who is serving as a patient care\r team physician dies, becomes disabled, retires from active practice, surrenders\r his license or has it suspended or revoked by the Board, or relocates his\r practice such that he is no longer able to serve, and an advanced practice\r registered nurse is unable to enter into a new practice agreement with another\r patient care team physician, the advanced practice registered nurse may\r continue to practice upon notification to the designee or his alternate of the\r Boards and receipt of such notification. Such advanced practice registered\r nurse may continue to treat patients without a patient care team physician for\r an initial period not to exceed 60 days, provided that the advanced practice registered\r nurse continues to prescribe only those drugs previously authorized by the\r practice agreement with such physician and to have access to appropriate input\r from appropriate health care providers in complex clinical cases and patient\r emergencies and for referrals. The designee or his alternate of the Boards\r shall grant permission for the advanced practice registered nurse to continue\r practice under this subsection for another 60 days, provided that the advanced\r practice registered nurse provides evidence of efforts made to secure another\r patient care team physician and of access to physician input.</p>\r \r <p>H. Every certified nurse midwife shall practice in accordance\r with regulations adopted by the Boards and consistent with the Standards for\r the Practice of Midwifery set by the American College of Nurse-Midwives\r governing such practice. A certified nurse midwife who has practiced fewer than\r 1,000 hours shall practice in consultation with a certified nurse midwife who\r has practiced for at least two years prior to entering into the practice\r agreement or a licensed physician, in accordance with a practice agreement.\r Such practice agreement shall address the availability of the certified nurse\r midwife who has practiced for at least two years prior to entering into the\r practice agreement or the licensed physician for routine and urgent\r consultation on patient care. Evidence of the practice agreement shall be\r maintained by the certified nurse midwife and provided to the Boards upon\r request. A certified nurse midwife who has completed 1,000 hours of practice as\r a certified nurse midwife may practice without a practice agreement upon\r receipt by the certified nurse midwife of an attestation from the certified\r nurse midwife who has practiced for at least two years prior to entering into\r the practice agreement or the licensed physician with whom the certified nurse\r midwife has entered into a practice agreement stating (i) that such certified\r nurse midwife or licensed physician has provided consultation to the certified\r nurse midwife pursuant to a practice agreement meeting the requirements of this\r section and (ii) the period of time for which such certified nurse midwife or\r licensed physician practiced in collaboration and consultation with the\r certified nurse midwife pursuant to the practice agreement. A certified nurse\r midwife authorized to practice without a practice agreement shall consult and\r collaborate with and refer patients to such other health care providers as may\r be appropriate for the care of the patient.</p>\r \r <p>I. A nurse practitioner who has completed the equivalent of at\r least five years of full-time clinical experience, as determined by the Boards,\r may practice in the practice category in which he is certified and licensed\r without a written or electronic practice agreement upon receipt by the nurse\r practitioner of an attestation from the patient care team physician stating (i)\r that the patient care team physician has served as a patient care team\r physician on a patient care team with the nurse practitioner pursuant to a\r practice agreement meeting the requirements of this section and § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957.01\">54.1-2957.01</a>;\r (ii) that while a party to such practice agreement, the patient care team\r physician routinely practiced with a patient population and in a practice area\r included within the category for which the nurse practitioner was certified and\r licensed; and (iii) the period of time for which the patient care team\r physician practiced with the nurse practitioner under such a practice\r agreement. A copy of such attestation shall be submitted to the Boards together\r with a fee established by the Boards. Upon receipt of such attestation and\r verification that a nurse practitioner satisfies the requirements of this\r subsection, the Boards shall issue to the nurse practitioner a new license that\r includes a designation indicating that the nurse practitioner is authorized to\r practice without a practice agreement. In the event that a nurse practitioner\r is unable to obtain the attestation required by this subsection, the Boards may\r accept other evidence demonstrating that the applicant has met the requirements\r of this subsection in accordance with regulations adopted by the Boards.</p>\r \r <p>A nurse practitioner authorized to practice without a practice\r agreement pursuant to this subsection shall (a) only practice within the scope\r of his clinical and professional training and limits of his knowledge and\r experience and consistent with the applicable standards of care, (b) consult\r and collaborate with other health care providers based on the clinical\r conditions of the patient to whom health care is provided, and (c) establish a\r plan for referral of complex medical cases and emergencies to physicians or\r other appropriate health care providers.</p>\r \r <p>J. A clinical nurse specialist licensed by the Boards of\r Medicine and Nursing who does not prescribe controlled substances or devices\r may practice in the practice category in which he is certified and licensed\r without a written or electronic practice agreement. Such clinical nurse\r specialist shall (i) only practice within the scope of his clinical and\r professional training and limits of his knowledge and experience and consistent\r with the applicable standards of care, (ii) consult and collaborate with other\r health care providers based on the clinical condition of the patient to whom\r health care is provided, and (iii) establish a plan for referral of complex\r medical cases and emergencies to physicians or other appropriate health care\r providers.</p>\r \r <p>A clinical nurse specialist licensed by the Boards who\r prescribes controlled substances or devices shall practice in consultation with\r a licensed physician in accordance with a practice agreement between the\r clinical nurse specialist and the licensed physician. Such practice agreement\r shall address the availability of the physician for routine and urgent\r consultation on patient care. Evidence of a practice agreement shall be\r maintained by a clinical nurse specialist and provided to the Boards upon\r request. The practice of clinical nurse specialists shall be consistent with\r the standards of care for the profession and with applicable laws and\r regulations.</p>','FH1122',18,'senate','failed committee','failed',NULL,'<p>According to the Fiscal Impact Statement, this legislation is estimated to have a minimal fiscal impact. There would be costs associated with the Board of Medicine and the Board of Nursing to promulgate regulations, but these costs can be handled within existing resources. No specific agency or political subdivisions are mentioned as being affected by this legislation.</p><p>Summary generated automatically by OpenAI.</p>','a1df0b8d0a2e15fd78259a783f36c74d',126,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-11','2024-11-17 00:55:08','2024-01-11 16:55:02');
