INSERT INTO `bills` VALUES
(73112,'hb159',30,'house','State correctional and juvenile correctional facilities; use of canines, prohibited acts.',492,'<b>Use of canines in correctional and juvenile correctional facilities; prohibited acts.</b> Makes it unlawful for any correctional officer or other employee of a state correctional facility who is permitted to handle canines to use a patrol or security canine in any state correctional facility unless such correctional officer or other employee (i) reasonably believes that the use of a patrol or security canine is immediately necessary to protect any prisoner or any officer or employee from the threat of serious bodily injury or death or (ii) has the prior approval of the warden or a supervisor to use a patrol or security canine to intervene in an altercation, fight, or other incident between three or more prisoners. The bill also makes it unlawful for any juvenile correctional officer or other employee of a juvenile correctional facility to use a patrol or security canine in any juvenile correctional facility. The bill specifies that such provisions shall not apply to the training or use of detector canines or detector canine handlers.','<br><center><b>VIRGINIA ACTS OF ASSEMBLY -- CHAPTER</b></center>\r \r <i>An Act to amend the Code of Virginia by adding sections\r numbered <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/53.1-39.3\">53.1-39.3</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/66-21.1\">66-21.1</a>, relating to use of canines in state\r correctional and juvenile correctional facilities; prohibited acts.</i>\r \r <center>[H 159]</center>\r \r <center>Approved</center>\r \r <p> </p>\r \r <p>Be it enacted by the General Assembly of Virginia:</p>\r \r <p>1. That the Code of Virginia is amended by adding sections\r numbered <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/53.1-39.3\">53.1-39.3</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/66-21.1\">66-21.1</a> as follows:</p>\r \r <p><ins>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/53.1-39.3\">53.1-39.3</a>. Use of canines in state correctional\r facilities; prohibited acts; policies and regulations made public; incidents of\r use of canines reported; exception.</ins></p>\r \r <p><ins>A. It is unlawful for any correctional officer or other\r employee of a state correctional facility who is permitted to handle canines to\r use a patrol or security canine in any state correctional facility unless such\r correctional officer or other employee (i) reasonably believes that the use of\r a patrol or security canine is immediately necessary to protect any prisoner or\r any officer or employee from the threat of serious bodily injury or death or\r (ii) has the prior approval of the warden or a supervisor to use a patrol or\r security canine to intervene in an altercation, fight, or other incident\r between three or more prisoners. If feasible, the correctional officer shall\r provide a warning to the subject of any canine use of force prior to the\r deployment of a canine.</ins></p>\r \r <p><ins>B. The Department shall make public any policies and\r regulations relating to (i) the use of canines, (ii) training requirements for\r both canines and the handlers of such canines, and (iii) the supervision of the\r officers or employees who are permitted to handle such canines.</ins></p>\r \r <p><ins>C. The Department shall track all canine uses of force and\r all incidents in which canines were present or requested for assistance but no\r canine use of force occurred. The information collected shall be reported\r publicly and made available on the Department\'s website.</ins></p>\r \r <p><ins>D. The provisions of this section shall not apply to the\r training or use of detector canines or detector canine handlers.</ins></p>\r \r <p><ins>E. Nothing in this section shall be construed as\r prohibiting the use of a canine to locate a prisoner who has escaped from a\r state correctional facility.</ins></p>\r \r <p><ins>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/66-21.1\">66-21.1</a>. Use of canines in juvenile correctional\r facilities; prohibited acts; exception.</ins></p>\r \r <p><ins>A. It is unlawful for any juvenile correctional officer or\r other employee of a juvenile correctional facility to use a patrol or security\r canine in any juvenile correctional facility.</ins></p>\r \r <p><ins>B. The provisions of this section shall not apply to the\r training or use of detector canines or detector canine handlers.</ins></p>\r \r <p><ins>C. Nothing in this section shall be construed as\r prohibiting the use of a canine to locate a juvenile who has escaped from a\r juvenile correctional facility.</ins></p>','FER122',2,'house','signed by governor','passed',NULL,'<p>Based on the <a href=\"https://lis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+oth+HB159F122+PDF\">fiscal impact statement</a>, it is unclear what the exact cost of the legislation will be. The Department of Corrections (DOC) is currently reviewing the impact of the bill on agency operations, but it is possible that any fiscal impact could be addressed using current resources. The Department of Juvenile Justice states that the bill will have no fiscal impact on agency operations as they do not use security canines. The impact on local and regional jails is unknown at this time. The Office of the Attorney General believes that the bill may expose the Commonwealth to additional litigation, but the exact fiscal impact cannot be quantified at this time.</p>\n        <p class=\"openai\">Summary generated automatically by OpenAI.</p>','5efed59f705e1068f7ead2a8be3be71c',112,0,4,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-02','2024-11-17 00:55:04','2024-01-02 22:55:02');
