INSERT INTO `bills` VALUES
(76741,'sb124',31,'senate','Sports betting; permitted on Virginia college sports.',439,'<b>Sports betting; Virginia college sports.</b> Permits betting, with the exception of proposition betting, on Virginia college sports. Under current law, betting other than proposition betting is allowed on all college sports except Virginia college sports.','SENATE BILL NO. 124\r </b></center>\r <center>\r Offered January 10, 2024\r </center>\r <center>\r Prefiled January 4, 2024\r </center>\r <i>A BILL to amend and reenact §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4030\">58.1-4030</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4039\">58.1-4039</a> of the \r  Code of Virginia and the fourth enactment of Chapter 1197 and the fourth enactment \r  of Chapter 1248 of the Acts of Assembly of 2020, relating to sports \r  betting; Virginia college sports.</i>\r <center>----------</center>\r <center>\r Patron-- VanValkenburg\r </center>\r <center>----------</center>\r <center>\r Referred to Committee on General Laws and Technology\r </center>\r <center>----------</center>\r  \r   <p>Be it enacted by the General Assembly of Virginia:</p>\r  \r   <p>1. That §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4030\">58.1-4030</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4039\">58.1-4039</a> of the Code of Virginia \r  are amended and reenacted as follows:</p>\r  \r   <p>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4030\">58.1-4030</a>. Definitions.</p>\r  \r   <p>As used in this article, unless the context requires a \r  different meaning:</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Adjusted gross revenue\" means gross revenue minus:</p>\r  \r   <p>1. All cash and the cash value of merchandise paid out as \r  winnings to bettors, and the value of all bonuses or promotions provided to \r  patrons as an incentive to place or as a result of their having placed Internet \r  sports betting wagers;</p>\r  \r   <p>2. Uncollectible gaming receivables, which shall not exceed \r  two percent, or a different percentage as determined by the Board pursuant to \r  subsection F of § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4007\">58.1-4007</a>, of gross revenue minus all cash paid out as \r  winnings to bettors;</p>\r  \r   <p>3. If the permit holder is a significant infrastructure \r  limited licensee, as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/59.1-365\">59.1-365</a>, any funds paid into the horsemen\'s \r  purse account pursuant to the provisions of subdivision 14 of § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/59.1-369\">59.1-369</a>; and</p>\r  \r   <p>4. All excise taxes on sports betting paid pursuant to federal \r  law.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Amateur sports\" means any sports or athletic event \r  that is not professional sports, college sports,<s> Virginia \r  college sports,</s> or youth sports. \r  \"Amateur sports\" includes domestic, international, and Olympic sports \r  or athletic events. \"Amateur sports\" does not include charitable \r  gaming, as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/18.2-340.16\">18.2-340.16</a>; fantasy contests, as defined in § \r  <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/59.1-556\">59.1-556</a>; or horse racing, as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/59.1-365\">59.1-365</a>.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"College sports\" means an athletic event<s> (i)</s> in which at least one \r  participant is a team from a public or private institution of higher education, \r  regardless of where such institution is located<s>, \r  and (ii) that does not include a team from a Virginia public or private \r  institution of higher education</s>.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Covered persons\" means athletes; umpires, referees, \r  and officials; personnel associated with clubs, teams, leagues, and athletic \r  associations; medical professionals and athletic trainers who provide services \r  to athletes and players; and the immediate family members and associates of \r  such persons.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Gross revenue\" means the total of all cash, \r  property, or any other form of remuneration, whether collected or not, received \r  by a permittee from its sports betting operations.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Major league sports franchise\" means a professional \r  baseball, basketball, football, hockey, or soccer team that is at the \r  highest-level league of play for its respective sport.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Motor sports facility\" means an outdoor motor \r  sports facility that hosts a National Association for Stock Car Auto Racing \r  (NASCAR) national touring race.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Official league data\" means statistics, results, \r  outcomes, and other data relating to a professional sports event obtained by a \r  permit holder under an agreement with a sports governing body or with an entity \r  expressly authorized by a sports governing body for determining the outcome of \r  tier 2 bets.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Permit holder\" means a person to which the Director \r  issues a permit pursuant to §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4032\">58.1-4032</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4033\">58.1-4033</a>.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Personal biometric data\" means any information \r  about an athlete that is derived from his DNA, heart rate, blood pressure, \r  perspiration rate, internal or external body temperature, hormone levels, \r  glucose levels, hydration levels, vitamin levels, bone density, muscle density, \r  or sleep patterns, or other information as may be prescribed by the Board by \r  regulation.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Principal\" means any individual who solely or \r  together with his immediate family members (i) owns or controls, directly or \r  indirectly, five percent or more of the pecuniary interest in any entity that \r  is a permit holder or (ii) has the power to vote or cause the vote of five \r  percent or more of the voting securities or other ownership interests of such \r  entity. \"Principal\" includes any individual who is employed in a \r  managerial capacity for a sports betting platform or sports betting facility on \r  behalf of a permit holder.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Professional sports\" means an athletic event \r  involving at least two human competitors who receive compensation, in excess of \r  their expenses, for participating in such event. \"Professional \r  sports\" does not include charitable gaming, as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/18.2-340.16\">18.2-340.16</a>; \r  fantasy contests, as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/59.1-556\">59.1-556</a>; or horse racing, as defined in § \r  <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/59.1-365\">59.1-365</a>.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Prohibited conduct\" means any statement, action, or \r  other communication intended to influence, manipulate, or control a betting \r  outcome of a sports event or of any individual occurrence or performance in a \r  sports event in exchange for financial gain or to avoid financial or physical \r  harm. \"Prohibited conduct\" includes statements, actions, and \r  communications made to a covered person by a third party. \"Prohibited \r  conduct\" does not include statements, actions, or communications made or \r  sanctioned by a sports team or sports governing body.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Proposition bet\" means a bet on an individual \r  action, statistic, occurrence, or non-occurrence to be determined during an \r  athletic event and includes any such action, statistic, occurrence, or \r  non-occurrence that does not directly affect the final outcome of the athletic event \r  to which it relates.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Sports betting\" means placing wagers on \r  professional sports, college sports, amateur sports, sporting events, or any \r  other event approved by the Director, and any portion thereof, and includes \r  placing wagers related to the individual performance statistics of athletes in \r  such sports and events. \"Sports betting\" includes any system or \r  method of wagering approved by the Director, including single-game bets, teaser \r  bets, parlays, over-under, moneyline, pools, exchange wagering, in-game \r  wagering, in-play bets, proposition bets, and straight bets. \"Sports \r  betting\" does not include participating in charitable gaming authorized by \r  Article 1.1:1 (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/18.2-340.15\">18.2-340.15</a> et seq.) of Chapter 8 of Title 18.2; participating \r  in any lottery game authorized under Article 1 (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4000\">58.1-4000</a> et seq.); wagering \r  on horse racing authorized by Chapter 29 (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/59.1-364\">59.1-364</a> et seq.) of Title 59.1; or \r  participating in fantasy contests authorized by Chapter 51 (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/59.1-556\">59.1-556</a> et seq.) \r  of Title 59.1.<s> \"Sports \r  betting\" does not include placing a wager on a college sports event in \r  which a Virginia public or private institution of higher education is a \r  participant.</s></p>\r  \r   <p>\"Sports betting facility\" means an area, kiosk, or \r  device located inside a casino gaming establishment licensed pursuant to \r  Chapter 41 (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4100\">58.1-4100</a> et seq.) that is designated for sports betting.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Sports betting permit\" means a permit to operate a \r  sports betting platform or sports betting facility issued pursuant to the \r  provisions of §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4032\">58.1-4032</a>, <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4033\">58.1-4033</a>, and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4034\">58.1-4034</a>.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Sports betting platform\" means a website, app, or \r  other platform accessible via the Internet or mobile, wireless, or similar \r  communications technology that sports bettors use to participate in sports \r  betting.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Sports betting program\" means the program established \r  by the Board to allow sports betting as described in this article.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Sports bettor\" means a person physically located in \r  Virginia who participates in sports betting.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Sports event\" or \"sporting event\" means \r  professional sports, college sports, amateur sports, and any athletic event, \r  motor race event, electronic sports event, competitive video game event, or any \r  other event approved by the Director.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Sports governing body\" means an organization, \r  headquartered in the United States, that prescribes rules and enforces codes of \r  conduct with respect to a professional sports or college sports event and the \r  participants therein. \"Sports governing body\" includes a designee of \r  the sports governing body.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Stadium\" means the physical facility that is the \r  primary location at which a major league sports franchise hosts athletic events \r  and any appurtenant facilities.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Tier 1 bet\" means a bet that is placed using the \r  Internet and that is not a tier 2 bet.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Tier 2 bet\" means a bet that is placed using the \r  Internet and that is placed after the event it concerns has started.</p>\r  \r   <p><s>\"Virginia \r  college sports\" means an athletic event in which at least one participant \r  is a team from a Virginia public or private institution of higher education.</s></p>\r  \r   <p>\"Youth sports\" means an athletic event (i) involving \r  a majority of participants under age 18 or (ii) in which at least one \r  participant is a team from a public or private elementary, middle, or secondary \r  school, regardless of where such school is located. However, if an athletic \r  event meets the definition of college sports or professional sports, such event \r  shall not be considered youth sports regardless of the age of the participants. \r  An international athletic event organized by the International Olympic \r  Committee shall not be considered to be youth sports, regardless of the age of \r  the participants.</p>\r  \r   <p>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4039\">58.1-4039</a>. Events on which betting is prohibited; penalty.</p>\r  \r   <p>A. 1. No person shall place or accept a bet on youth sports.</p>\r  \r   <p>2. No person shall place or accept a proposition bet on \r  college sports.</p>\r  \r   <p><s>3. No person shall \r  place or accept a bet on Virginia college sports.</s></p>\r  \r   <p>B. 1. A sports governing body may notify the Department that \r  it desires to restrict, limit, or prohibit sports betting on its sporting \r  events by providing notice in accordance with requirements prescribed by the \r  Director. A sports governing body also may request to restrict the types of \r  bets that may be offered. Notwithstanding § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4030\">58.1-4030</a>, for purposes of this \r  section, \"sports governing body\" includes any organization that is \r  not headquartered in the United States and that otherwise meets the definition \r  of \"sports governing body.\"</p>\r  \r   <p>2. For any request made pursuant to subdivision 1, the \r  requester shall bear the burden of establishing to the satisfaction of the \r  Director that the relevant betting or other activity poses a significant and \r  unreasonable integrity risk. The Director shall seek input from affected permit \r  holders before making a determination on such request.</p>\r  \r   <p>3. If the Director denies a request made pursuant to \r  subdivision 1, the Director shall give the requester notice and the right to be \r  heard and offer proof in opposition to such determination in accordance with \r  regulations established by the Board. If the Director grants a request, the \r  Board shall promulgate by regulation such restrictions, limitations, or \r  prohibitions as may be requested.</p>\r  \r   <p>4. A permit holder shall not offer or take any bets in \r  violation of regulations promulgated by the Board pursuant to this subsection.</p>\r  \r   <p>C. The<s> prohibitions</s><ins> prohibition</ins> in<s> subdivisions</s><ins> subdivision</ins> A 1<s> and \r  A 3</s> shall be limited to the \r  single game or match in which a youth sports<s> or \r  Virginia college sports</s> team is \r  a participant. The<s> prohibitions</s><ins> prohibition</ins> shall not be construed to prohibit betting on other games \r  in a tournament or multigame event in which a youth sports<s> or \r  Virginia college sports</s> team \r  participates, so long as such other games do not have a participant that is a \r  youth sports<s> or \r  Virginia college sports</s> team.</p>\r  \r   <p>D. Any person convicted of violating this section is guilty of \r  a Class 1 misdemeanor.</p>\r  \r   <p>2. That the fourth enactment of Chapter 1197 and the fourth enactment \r  of Chapter 1248 of the Acts of Assembly of 2020 are amended and \r  reenacted as follows:</p>\r  \r   <p><b>4. That if the Virginia Lottery (the Lottery) administers a \r  program under which the Lottery issues licenses or permits to operate online \r  sports betting platforms or sports betting facilities, the Lottery shall issue \r  any such licenses or permits to any casino gaming operator licensed under \r  Article 3 (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4108\">58.1-4108</a> et seq.) of Chapter 41 of Title 58.1 of the Code of \r  Virginia, as created by this act, regardless of whether such casino gaming \r  operator otherwise meets the requirements for obtaining such license or permit. \r  Any casino gaming operator receiving a license or permit to operate an online \r  sports betting platform and a sports betting facility pursuant to the \r  provisions of this enactment shall be subject to all Virginia statutory or \r  regulatory laws governing sports betting, including: (i) laws defining sports \r  betting and prohibiting any activities related thereto; (ii) fees for \r  applications, licenses, and permits, and any other payments required by the \r  Lottery; and (iii) taxes for offering sports betting.<s> Notwithstanding \r  any law to the contrary, a casino gaming operator receiving a license or permit \r  to operate an online sports betting platform or a sports betting facility \r  pursuant to the provisions of this enactment shall not allow wagering on any \r  athletic event in which at least one participant is a team from a Virginia \r  public or private institution of higher education.</s> Any license or permit issued pursuant to the provisions \r  of this enactment shall expire whenever the casino gaming operator is no longer \r  licensed under Article 3 (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/58.1-4108\">58.1-4108</a> et seq.) of Chapter 41 of Title 58.1 of \r  the Code of Virginia, as created by this act.</b></p>','241F122',19,'senate','introduced','failed',NULL,NULL,'113916da5195aca667c6f72c3ae7a596',105,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-04','2026-01-25 21:34:27','2024-11-17 01:55:21');
