INSERT INTO `bills` VALUES
(73230,'hb224',30,'house','Public schools; mental health awareness training.',508,'<b>Public schools; teachers and other relevant personnel; mental health awareness training.</b> Requires each teacher and other relevant personnel, as determined by the applicable school board, employed on a full-time basis to complete mental health awareness training that addresses the needs of youth populations that are at a high risk of experiencing mental health challenges and disorders in accordance with evidence-based best practices developed by the American Psychological Association. Current law requires such teachers and personnel to complete mental health awareness training but does not contain any requirements relating to the specific topics such training must address. The bill prohibits any of its provisions or any policy adopted in accordance with its provisions from being construed to permit biased or discriminatory treatment of any youth population deemed to be at a high risk of experiencing mental health challenges and disorders.','<br><center><b>VIRGINIA ACTS OF ASSEMBLY -- CHAPTER</b></center>\r \r <i>An Act to amend and reenact § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/22.1-298.6\">22.1-298.6</a> of the Code of\r Virginia, relating to public schools; mental health awareness training and\r instruction; requirements.</i>\r \r <center>[H 224]</center>\r \r <center>Approved</center>\r \r <p> </p>\r \r <p>Be it enacted by the General Assembly of Virginia:</p>\r \r <p>1. That § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/22.1-298.6\">22.1-298.6</a> of the Code of Virginia is amended and\r reenacted as follows:</p>\r \r <p>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/22.1-298.6\">22.1-298.6</a>. Mental health awareness training.</p>\r \r <p>A. Each school board shall adopt and implement policies that\r require each teacher and other relevant personnel, as determined by the school\r board, employed on a full-time basis, to complete a mental health awareness\r training or similar program at least once.<ins> Any such mental health awareness\r training or similar program shall address the needs of youth populations that\r are at a high risk of experiencing mental health challenges and disorders in\r accordance with evidence-based best practices developed by the American\r Psychological Association, including youth who (i) are bereaved by suicide;\r (ii) have mental or physical disabilities or chronic health conditions,\r including substance use disorders; (iii) are experiencing homelessness or\r housing instability; (iv) are in foster care or other situations that may\r result in instability in a youth\'s custodial or living situation; or (v)\r identify as LGBTQ+. The provisions of this section or any policy adopted in\r accordance with the provisions of this section shall not be construed to permit\r biased or discriminatory treatment of any youth population deemed to be at a\r high risk of experiencing mental health challenges and disorders.</ins></p>\r \r <p>B. Each school board shall provide required personnel the\r training required by subsection A and may contract with the Department of\r Behavioral Health and Developmental Services, a community services board, a\r behavioral health authority, a nonprofit organization, or other certified\r trainer as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/37.2-312.2\">37.2-312.2</a> to provide such training. Such training may\r be provided via an online module.</p>','FER122',6,'house','vetoed by governor','failed',NULL,'<p>The <a href=\"https://lis.virginia.gov/cgi-bin/legp604.exe?241+oth+HB224FH1122+PDF\">fiscal impact statement</a> states that there is no anticipated state fiscal impact resulting from this bill. However, the impact on local school divisions is indeterminate.</p>\n        <p class=\"openai\">Summary generated automatically by OpenAI.</p>','a32298a1d839f944d36a68f849285c53',96,0,1,NULL,NULL,NULL,'2024-01-04','2024-11-17 00:55:04','2024-01-04 17:55:02');
