(1097265,74616,'CHAP0548',30,'2024-04-05',NULL,NULL,20,'2024-04-23 15:55:02','2025-11-06 00:15:32'),
(1028767,74616,'HB1278',30,'2024-01-10','HOUSE BILL NO. 1278\r </b></center>\r <center>\r Offered January 10, 2024\r </center>\r <center>\r Prefiled January 10, 2024\r </center>\r <i>A BILL to amend and reenact §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a> of the \r  Code of Virginia, relating to auricular acupuncture; \r  use of the five needle protocol.</i>\r <center>----------</center>\r <center>\r Patron-- Zehr\r </center>\r <center>----------</center>\r <center>\r Committee Referral Pending\r </center>\r <center>----------</center>\r  \r   <p>Be it enacted by the General Assembly of Virginia:</p>\r  \r   <p>1. That §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a> of the Code of Virginia \r  are amended and reenacted as follows:</p>\r  \r   <p>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a>. Definitions.</p>\r  \r   <p>As used in this chapter, unless the context requires a \r  different meaning:</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Acupuncturist\" means an individual approved by the \r  Board to practice acupuncture. This is limited to \"licensed \r  acupuncturist\" which means an individual other than a doctor of medicine, \r  osteopathy, chiropractic or podiatry who has successfully completed the \r  requirements for licensure established by the Board (approved titles are \r  limited to: Licensed Acupuncturist, Lic.Ac., and L.Ac.).</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Advanced practice registered nurse\" means a \r  certified nurse midwife, certified registered nurse anesthetist, clinical nurse \r  specialist, or nurse practitioner who is jointly licensed by the Boards of \r  Medicine and Nursing pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>, has completed an advanced \r  graduate-level education program in a specialty category of nursing, and has \r  passed a national certifying examination for that specialty.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Auricular acupuncture\" means the subcutaneous \r  insertion of sterile, disposable acupuncture needles in predetermined, \r  bilateral locations in the outer ear when used exclusively and specifically in \r  the context of a chemical dependency treatment program<ins> or \r  for the treatment of behavioral health conditions</ins>.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Birth control\" means contraceptive methods that are \r  approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. \"Birth control\" \r  shall not be considered abortion for the purposes of Title 18.2.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Board\" means the Board of Medicine.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Certified nurse midwife\" means an advanced practice \r  registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of nurse midwifery and who \r  is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as an advanced \r  practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Certified registered nurse anesthetist\" means an \r  advanced practice registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of nurse \r  anesthesia, who is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as an \r  advanced practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>, and who practices \r  under the supervision of a doctor of medicine, osteopathy, podiatry, or \r  dentistry but is not subject to the practice agreement requirement described in \r  § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Clinical nurse specialist\" means an advanced \r  practice registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of clinical nurse \r  specialist and who is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as \r  an advanced practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Collaboration\" means the communication and \r  decision-making process among health care providers who are members of a \r  patient care team related to the treatment of a patient that includes the \r  degree of cooperation necessary to provide treatment and care of the patient \r  and includes (i) communication of data and information about the treatment and \r  care of a patient, including the exchange of clinical observations and \r  assessments, and (ii) development of an appropriate plan of care, including \r  decisions regarding the health care provided, accessing and assessment of appropriate \r  additional resources or expertise, and arrangement of appropriate referrals, \r  testing, or studies.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Consultation\" means communicating data and \r  information, exchanging clinical observations and assessments, accessing and \r  assessing additional resources and expertise, problem-solving, and arranging \r  for referrals, testing, or studies.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Genetic counselor\" means a person licensed by the \r  Board to engage in the practice of genetic counseling.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Healing arts\" means the arts and sciences dealing \r  with the prevention, diagnosis, treatment and cure or alleviation of human \r  physical or mental ailments, conditions, diseases, pain or infirmities.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Licensed certified midwife\" means a person who is \r  licensed as a certified midwife by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Medical malpractice judgment\" means any final order \r  of any court entering judgment against a licensee of the Board that arises out \r  of any tort action or breach of contract action for personal injuries or \r  wrongful death, based on health care or professional services rendered, or that \r  should have been rendered, by a health care provider, to a patient.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Medical malpractice settlement\" means any written \r  agreement and release entered into by or on behalf of a licensee of the Board \r  in response to a written claim for money damages that arises out of any \r  personal injuries or wrongful death, based on health care or professional \r  services rendered, or that should have been rendered, by a health care \r  provider, to a patient.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Nurse practitioner\" means an advanced practice registered \r  nurse, other than an advanced practice registered nurse licensed by the Boards \r  of Medicine and Nursing in the category of certified nurse midwife, certified \r  registered nurse anesthetist, or clinical nurse specialist, who is jointly \r  licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Occupational therapy assistant\" means an individual \r  who has met the requirements of the Board for licensure and who works under the \r  supervision of a licensed occupational therapist to assist in the practice of \r  occupational therapy.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Patient care team\" means a multidisciplinary team \r  of health care providers actively functioning as a unit with the management and \r  leadership of one or more patient care team physicians for the purpose of \r  providing and delivering health care to a patient or group of patients.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Patient care team physician\" means a physician who \r  is actively licensed to practice medicine in the Commonwealth, who regularly \r  practices medicine in the Commonwealth, and who provides management and leadership \r  in the care of patients as part of a patient care team.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Patient care team podiatrist\" means a podiatrist \r  who is actively licensed to practice podiatry in the Commonwealth, who \r  regularly practices podiatry in the Commonwealth, and who provides management \r  and leadership in the care of patients as part of a patient care team.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Physician assistant\" means a health care \r  professional who has met the requirements of the Board for licensure as a \r  physician assistant.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of acupuncture\" means the stimulation of \r  certain points on or near the surface of the body by the insertion of needles \r  to prevent or modify the perception of pain or to normalize physiological \r  functions, including pain control, for the treatment of certain ailments or \r  conditions of the body and includes the techniques of electroacupuncture, \r  cupping<ins>,</ins> and moxibustion. The practice \r  of acupuncture does not include the use of physical therapy, chiropractic, or \r  osteopathic manipulative techniques; the use or prescribing of any drugs, \r  medications, serums or vaccines; or the procedure of auricular acupuncture as \r  exempted in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a> when used in the context of a chemical dependency \r  treatment program<ins> or for the \r  treatment of behavioral health conditions</ins> for patients eligible for federal, state<ins>,</ins> or local public funds by an \r  employee of the program who is trained and approved by the National Acupuncture \r  Detoxification Association or an equivalent certifying body.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of athletic training\" means the prevention, \r  recognition, evaluation, and treatment of injuries or conditions related to \r  athletic or recreational activity that requires physical skill and utilizes \r  strength, power, endurance, speed, flexibility, range of motion or agility or a \r  substantially similar injury or condition resulting from occupational activity \r  immediately upon the onset of such injury or condition; and subsequent \r  treatment and rehabilitation of such injuries or conditions under the direction \r  of the patient\'s physician or under the direction of any doctor of medicine, \r  osteopathy, chiropractic, podiatry, or dentistry, while using heat, light, \r  sound, cold, electricity, exercise or mechanical or other devices.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of behavior analysis\" means the design, \r  implementation, and evaluation of environmental modifications, using behavioral \r  stimuli and consequences, to produce socially significant improvement in human \r  behavior, including the use of direct observation, measurement, and functional \r  analysis of the relationship between environment and behavior.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of chiropractic\" means the adjustment of \r  the 24 movable vertebrae of the spinal column, and assisting nature for the \r  purpose of normalizing the transmission of nerve energy, but does not include \r  the use of surgery, obstetrics, osteopathy, or the administration or \r  prescribing of any drugs, medicines, serums, or vaccines. \"Practice of \r  chiropractic\"<s> shall include</s><ins> includes</ins> (i) requesting, \r  receiving, and reviewing a patient\'s medical and physical history, including \r  information related to past surgical and nonsurgical treatment of the patient \r  and controlled substances prescribed to the patient, and (ii) documenting in a \r  patient\'s record information related to the condition and symptoms of the \r  patient, the examination and evaluation of the patient made by the doctor of \r  chiropractic, and treatment provided to the patient by the doctor of \r  chiropractic. \"Practice of chiropractic\"<s> shall</s> \r  also<s> include</s><ins> \r  includes</ins> performing the physical examination of an \r  applicant for a commercial driver\'s license or commercial learner\'s permit \r  pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/46.2-341.12\">46.2-341.12</a> if the practitioner has<s> (i)</s><ins> (a)</ins> applied for and received \r  certification as a medical examiner pursuant to 49 C.F.R. Part 390, Subpart D \r  and<s> (ii)</s><ins> (b)</ins> \r  registered with the National Registry of Certified Medical Examiners.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of genetic counseling\" means (i) obtaining \r  and evaluating individual and family medical histories to assess the risk of \r  genetic medical conditions and diseases in a patient, his offspring, and other \r  family members; (ii) discussing the features, history, diagnosis, environmental \r  factors, and risk management of genetic medical conditions and diseases; (iii) \r  ordering genetic laboratory tests and other diagnostic studies necessary for \r  genetic assessment; (iv) integrating the results with personal and family \r  medical history to assess and communicate risk factors for genetic medical \r  conditions and diseases; (v) evaluating the patient\'s and family\'s responses to \r  the medical condition or risk of recurrence and providing client-centered counseling \r  and anticipatory guidance; (vi) identifying and utilizing community resources \r  that provide medical, educational, financial, and psychosocial support and \r  advocacy; and (vii) providing written documentation of medical, genetic, and \r  counseling information for families and health care professionals.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of licensed certified midwifery\" means the \r  provision of primary health care for preadolescents, adolescents, and adults \r  within the scope of practice of a certified midwife established in accordance \r  with the Standards for the Practice of Midwifery set by the American College of \r  Nurse-Midwives, including (i) providing sexual and reproductive care and care \r  during pregnancy and childbirth, postpartum care, and care for the newborn for \r  up to 28 days following the birth of the child; (ii) prescribing of \r  pharmacological and non-pharmacological therapies within the scope of the \r  practice of midwifery; (iii) consulting or collaborating with or referring \r  patients to such other health care providers as may be appropriate for the care \r  of the patients; and (iv) serving as an educator in the theory and practice of \r  midwifery.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of medicine or osteopathic medicine\" means \r  the prevention, diagnosis, and treatment of human physical or mental ailments, \r  conditions, diseases, pain, or infirmities by any means or method.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of occupational therapy\" means the \r  therapeutic use of occupations for habilitation and rehabilitation to enhance \r  physical health, mental health, and cognitive functioning and includes the evaluation, \r  analysis, assessment, and delivery of education and training in basic and \r  instrumental activities of daily living; the design, fabrication, and \r  application of orthoses (splints); the design, selection, and use of adaptive \r  equipment and assistive technologies; therapeutic activities to enhance \r  functional performance; vocational evaluation and training; and consultation \r  concerning the adaptation of physical, sensory, and social environments.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of podiatry\" means the prevention, \r  diagnosis, treatment, and cure or alleviation of physical conditions, diseases, \r  pain, or infirmities of the human foot and ankle, including the medical, \r  mechanical and surgical treatment of the ailments of the human foot and ankle, \r  but does not include amputation of the foot proximal to the transmetatarsal \r  level through the metatarsal shafts. Amputations proximal to the \r  metatarsal-phalangeal joints may only be performed in a hospital or ambulatory \r  surgery facility accredited by an organization listed in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2939\">54.1-2939</a>. The \r  practice includes the diagnosis and treatment of lower extremity ulcers; \r  however, the treatment of severe lower extremity ulcers proximal to the foot \r  and ankle may only be performed by appropriately trained, credentialed \r  podiatrists in an approved hospital or ambulatory surgery center at which the \r  podiatrist has privileges, as described in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2939\">54.1-2939</a>. The Board of Medicine \r  shall determine whether a specific type of treatment of the foot and ankle is \r  within the scope of practice of podiatry.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of radiologic technology\" means the \r  application of ionizing radiation to human beings for diagnostic or therapeutic \r  purposes.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of respiratory care\" means the (i) \r  administration of pharmacological, diagnostic, and therapeutic agents related \r  to respiratory care procedures necessary to implement a treatment, disease \r  prevention, pulmonary rehabilitative, or diagnostic regimen prescribed by a \r  practitioner of medicine or osteopathic medicine; (ii) transcription and \r  implementation of the written or verbal orders of a practitioner of medicine or \r  osteopathic medicine pertaining to the practice of respiratory care; (iii) \r  observation and monitoring of signs and symptoms, general behavior, general \r  physical response to respiratory care treatment and diagnostic testing, \r  including determination of whether such signs, symptoms, reactions, behavior or \r  general physical response exhibit abnormal characteristics; and (iv) \r  implementation of respiratory care procedures, based on observed abnormalities, \r  or appropriate reporting, referral, respiratory care protocols or changes in \r  treatment pursuant to the written or verbal orders by a licensed practitioner \r  of medicine or osteopathic medicine or the initiation of emergency procedures, \r  pursuant to the Board\'s regulations or as otherwise authorized by law. The \r  practice of respiratory care may be performed in any clinic, hospital, skilled \r  nursing facility, private dwelling or other place deemed appropriate by the \r  Board in accordance with the written or verbal order of a practitioner of \r  medicine or osteopathic medicine<s>,</s> \r  and shall be performed under qualified medical direction.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Practice of surgical assisting\" means the \r  performance of significant surgical tasks, including manipulation of organs, \r  suturing of tissue, placement of hemostatic agents, injection of local \r  anesthetic, harvesting of veins, implementation of devices, and other duties as \r  directed by a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, or podiatry under the \r  direct supervision of a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, or podiatry.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Qualified medical direction\" means, in the context \r  of the practice of respiratory care, having readily accessible to the \r  respiratory therapist a licensed practitioner of medicine or osteopathic \r  medicine who has specialty training or experience in the management of acute \r  and chronic respiratory disorders and who is responsible for the quality, \r  safety, and appropriateness of the respiratory services provided by the \r  respiratory therapist.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Radiologic technologist\" means an individual, other \r  than a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, podiatry, or chiropractic or a \r  dentist licensed pursuant to Chapter 27 (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2700\">54.1-2700</a> et seq.), who (i) \r  performs, may be called upon to perform, or is licensed to perform a \r  comprehensive scope of diagnostic or therapeutic radiologic procedures \r  employing ionizing radiation and (ii) is delegated or exercises responsibility \r  for the operation of radiation-generating equipment, the shielding of patient \r  and staff from unnecessary radiation, the appropriate exposure of radiographs, \r  the administration of radioactive chemical compounds under the direction of an \r  authorized user as specified by regulations of the Department of Health, or \r  other procedures that contribute to any significant extent to the site or \r  dosage of ionizing radiation to which a patient is exposed.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Radiologic technologist, limited\" means an \r  individual, other than a licensed radiologic technologist, dental hygienist, or \r  person who is otherwise authorized by the Board of Dentistry under Chapter 27 \r  (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2700\">54.1-2700</a> et seq.) and the regulations pursuant thereto, who performs \r  diagnostic radiographic procedures employing equipment that emits ionizing \r  radiation that is limited to specific areas of the human body.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Radiologist assistant\" means an individual who has \r  met the requirements of the Board for licensure as an advanced-level radiologic \r  technologist and who, under the direct supervision of a licensed doctor of \r  medicine or osteopathy specializing in the field of radiology, is authorized to \r  (i) assess and evaluate the physiological and psychological responsiveness of \r  patients undergoing radiologic procedures; (ii) evaluate image quality, make \r  initial observations, and communicate observations to the supervising \r  radiologist; (iii) administer contrast media or other medications prescribed by \r  the supervising radiologist; and (iv) perform, or assist the supervising \r  radiologist to perform, any other procedure consistent with the guidelines \r  adopted by the American College of Radiology, the American Society of \r  Radiologic Technologists, and the American Registry of Radiologic \r  Technologists.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Respiratory care\" means the practice of the allied \r  health profession responsible for the direct and indirect services, including \r  inhalation therapy and respiratory therapy, in the treatment, management, \r  diagnostic testing, control, and care of patients with deficiencies and \r  abnormalities associated with the cardiopulmonary system under qualified \r  medical direction.</p>\r  \r   <p>\"Surgical assistant\" means an individual who has met \r  the requirements of the Board for licensure as a surgical assistant and who \r  works under the direct supervision of a licensed doctor of medicine, \r  osteopathy, or podiatry.</p>\r  \r   <p>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a>. Exceptions and exemptions generally.</p>\r  \r   <p>A. The provisions of this chapter shall not prevent or \r  prohibit:</p>\r  \r   <p>1. Any person entitled to practice his profession under any \r  prior law on June 24, 1944, from continuing such practice within the scope of \r  the definition of his particular school of practice;</p>\r  \r   <p>2. Any person licensed to practice naturopathy prior to June \r  30, 1980, from continuing such practice in accordance with regulations \r  promulgated by the Board;</p>\r  \r   <p>3. Any licensed advanced practice registered nurse from \r  rendering care in accordance with the provisions of §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a> and \r  <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957.01\">54.1-2957.01</a>, any advanced practice registered nurse licensed by the Boards of \r  Medicine and Nursing in the category of certified nurse midwife practicing \r  pursuant to subsection H of § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>, or any advanced practice registered \r  nurse licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing in the category of \r  clinical nurse specialist practicing pursuant to subsection J of § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a> \r  when such services are authorized by regulations promulgated jointly by the \r  Boards of Medicine and Nursing;</p>\r  \r   <p>4. Any registered professional nurse, licensed advanced practice \r  registered nurse, graduate laboratory technician<ins>,</ins> \r  or other technical personnel who have been properly trained from rendering care \r  or services within the scope of their usual professional activities which shall \r  include the taking of blood, the giving of intravenous infusions and \r  intravenous injections, and the insertion of tubes when performed under the \r  orders of a person licensed to practice medicine or osteopathy, an advanced \r  practice registered nurse, or a physician assistant;</p>\r  \r   <p>5. Any dentist, pharmacist<ins>,</ins> \r  or optometrist from rendering care or services within the scope of his usual \r  professional activities;</p>\r  \r   <p>6. Any practitioner licensed or certified by the Board from \r  delegating to personnel supervised by him, such activities or functions as are \r  nondiscretionary and do not require the exercise of professional judgment for \r  their performance and which are usually or customarily delegated to such \r  persons by practitioners of the healing arts, if such activities or functions \r  are authorized by and performed for such practitioners of the healing arts and \r  responsibility for such activities or functions is assumed by such \r  practitioners of the healing arts;</p>\r  \r   <p>7. The rendering of medical advice or information through \r  telecommunications from a physician licensed to practice medicine in Virginia \r  or an adjoining state, or from a licensed advanced practice registered nurse, \r  to emergency medical personnel acting in an emergency situation;</p>\r  \r   <p>8. The domestic administration of family remedies;</p>\r  \r   <p>9. The giving or use of massages, steam baths, dry heat rooms, \r  infrared heat<ins>,</ins> or \r  ultraviolet lamps in public or private health clubs and spas;</p>\r  \r   <p>10. The manufacture or sale of proprietary medicines in this \r  Commonwealth by licensed pharmacists or druggists;</p>\r  \r   <p>11. The advertising or sale of commercial appliances or \r  remedies;</p>\r  \r   <p>12. The fitting by nonitinerant persons or manufacturers of \r  artificial eyes, limbs or other apparatus or appliances or the fitting of \r  plaster cast counterparts of deformed portions of the body by a nonitinerant \r  bracemaker or prosthetist for the purpose of having a three-dimensional record \r  of the deformity, when such bracemaker or prosthetist has received a \r  prescription from a licensed physician, licensed advanced practice registered \r  nurse, or licensed physician assistant directing the fitting of such casts and \r  such activities are conducted in conformity with the laws of Virginia;</p>\r  \r   <p>13. Any person from the rendering of first aid or medical \r  assistance in an emergency in the absence of a person licensed to practice \r  medicine or osteopathy under the provisions of this chapter;</p>\r  \r   <p>14. The practice of the religious tenets of any church in the \r  ministration to the sick and suffering by mental or spiritual means without the \r  use of any drug or material remedy, whether gratuitously or for compensation;</p>\r  \r   <p>15. Any legally qualified out-of-state or foreign practitioner \r  from meeting in consultation with legally licensed practitioners in this \r  Commonwealth;</p>\r  \r   <p>16. Any practitioner of the healing arts licensed or certified \r  and in good standing with the applicable regulatory agency in another state or \r  Canada when that practitioner of the healing arts is in Virginia temporarily \r  and such practitioner has been issued a temporary authorization by the Board \r  from practicing medicine or the duties of the profession for which he is \r  licensed or certified (i) in a summer camp or in conjunction with patients who \r  are participating in recreational activities, (ii) while participating in \r  continuing educational programs prescribed by the Board, or (iii) by rendering \r  at any site any health care services within the limits of his license, \r  voluntarily and without compensation, to any patient of any clinic which is \r  organized in whole or in part for the delivery of health care services without \r  charge as provided in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-106\">54.1-106</a>;</p>\r  \r   <p>17. The performance of the duties of any active duty health \r  care provider in active service in the army, navy, coast guard, marine corps, \r  air force, or public health service of the United States at any public or \r  private health care facility while such individual is so commissioned or \r  serving and in accordance with his official military duties;</p>\r  \r   <p>18. Any masseur, who publicly represents himself as such, from \r  performing services within the scope of his usual professional activities and \r  in conformance with state law;</p>\r  \r   <p>19. Any person from performing services in the lawful conduct \r  of his particular profession or business under state law;</p>\r  \r   <p>20. Any person from rendering emergency care pursuant to the \r  provisions of § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/8.01-225\">8.01-225</a>;</p>\r  \r   <p>21. Qualified emergency medical services personnel, when \r  acting within the scope of their certification, and licensed health care \r  practitioners, when acting within their scope of practice, from following \r  Durable Do Not Resuscitate Orders issued in accordance with § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2987.1\">54.1-2987.1</a> and \r  Board of Health regulations, or licensed health care practitioners from \r  following any other written order of a physician not to resuscitate a patient \r  in the event of cardiac or respiratory arrest;</p>\r  \r   <p>22. Any commissioned or contract medical officer of the army, \r  navy, coast guard or air force rendering services voluntarily and without \r  compensation while deemed to be licensed pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-106\">54.1-106</a>;</p>\r  \r   <p>23. Any provider of a chemical dependency treatment program \r  who is certified as an \"acupuncture detoxification specialist\" by the \r  National Acupuncture Detoxification Association or an equivalent certifying \r  body, from administering auricular acupuncture treatment under the appropriate \r  supervision of a National Acupuncture Detoxification Association certified \r  licensed physician or licensed acupuncturist;</p>\r  \r   <p>24.<ins> \r  Any person from engaging in the five needle auricular acupuncture protocol \r  (5NP), a standardized protocol wherein up to five needles are inserted into the \r  external human ear to provide relief from the effects of behavioral health \r  conditions, provided such person (i) has appropriate \r  training in the 5NP through the National \r  Acupuncture Detoxification Association, the People\'s Organization of Community \r  Acupuncture, or other equivalent certifying body; (ii) \r  does not indicate or imply that he is an acupuncturist; and \r  (iii) does not indicate or \r  imply that his practice of the 5NP is regulated by the Commonwealth. \r  Treatment utilizing the 5NP \r  pursuant to this subdivision is \r  limited to the insertion of disposable, sterile acupuncture needles into the external \r  ear;</ins></p>\r  \r   <p><ins>25.</ins> Any employee of any assisted living facility who is \r  certified in cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) acting in compliance with the \r  patient\'s individualized service plan and with the written order of the \r  attending physician not to resuscitate a patient in the event of cardiac or \r  respiratory arrest;</p>\r  \r   <p><s>25. </s><ins>26. </ins>Any person working as a \r  health assistant under the direction of a licensed medical or osteopathic \r  doctor within the Department of Corrections, the Department of Juvenile Justice \r  or local correctional facilities;</p>\r  \r   <p><s>26. </s><ins>27. </ins>Any employee of a school \r  board, authorized by a prescriber and trained in the administration of insulin \r  and glucagon, when, upon the authorization of a prescriber and the written \r  request of the parents as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/22.1-1\">22.1-1</a>, assisting with the \r  administration of insulin or administrating glucagon to a student diagnosed as \r  having diabetes and who requires insulin injections during the school day or \r  for whom glucagon has been prescribed for the emergency treatment of \r  hypoglycemia;</p>\r  \r   <p><s>27. </s><ins>28. </ins>Any practitioner of the \r  healing arts or other profession regulated by the Board from rendering free \r  health care to an underserved population of Virginia who (i) does not regularly \r  practice his profession in Virginia, (ii) holds a current valid license or \r  certificate to practice his profession in another state, territory, district or \r  possession of the United States, (iii) volunteers to provide free health care \r  to an underserved area of the Commonwealth under the auspices of a publicly \r  supported all volunteer, nonprofit organization that sponsors the provision of \r  health care to populations of underserved people, (iv) files a copy of the \r  license or certification issued in such other jurisdiction with the Board, (v) \r  notifies the Board at least five business days prior to the voluntary provision \r  of services of the dates and location of such service, and (vi) acknowledges, \r  in writing, that such licensure exemption shall only be valid, in compliance \r  with the Board\'s regulations, during the limited period that such free health \r  care is made available through the volunteer, nonprofit organization on the \r  dates and at the location filed with the Board. The Board may deny the right to \r  practice in Virginia to any practitioner of the healing arts whose license or \r  certificate has been previously suspended or revoked, who has been convicted of \r  a felony or who is otherwise found to be in violation of applicable laws or \r  regulations. However, the Board shall allow a practitioner of the healing arts \r  who meets the above criteria to provide volunteer services without prior notice \r  for a period of up to three days, provided the nonprofit organization verifies \r  that the practitioner has a valid, unrestricted license in another state;</p>\r  \r   <p><s>28. </s><ins>29. </ins>Any registered nurse, \r  acting as an agent of the Department of Health, from obtaining specimens of \r  sputum or other bodily fluid from persons in whom the diagnosis of active \r  tuberculosis disease, as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-49.1\">32.1-49.1</a>, is suspected and submitting \r  orders for testing of such specimens to the Division of Consolidated \r  Laboratories or other public health laboratories, designated by the State \r  Health Commissioner, for the purpose of determining the presence or absence of \r  tubercle bacilli as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-49.1\">32.1-49.1</a>;</p>\r  \r   <p><s>29. </s><ins>30. </ins>Any physician of medicine \r  or osteopathy or advanced practice registered nurse from delegating to a \r  registered nurse under his supervision the screening and testing of children \r  for elevated blood-lead levels when such testing is conducted (i) in accordance \r  with a written protocol between the physician or advanced practice registered \r  nurse and the registered nurse and (ii) in compliance with the Board of \r  Health\'s regulations promulgated pursuant to §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-46.1\">32.1-46.1</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-46.2\">32.1-46.2</a>. Any \r  follow-up testing or treatment shall be conducted at the direction of a \r  physician or an advanced practice registered nurse;</p>\r  \r   <p><s>30. </s><ins>31. </ins>Any practitioner of one of \r  the professions regulated by the Board of Medicine who is in good standing with \r  the applicable regulatory agency in another state or Canada from engaging in \r  the practice of that profession when the practitioner is in Virginia \r  temporarily with an out-of-state athletic team or athlete for the duration of \r  the athletic tournament, game, or event in which the team or athlete is \r  competing;</p>\r  \r   <p><s>31. </s><ins>32. </ins>Any person from performing \r  state or federally funded health care tasks directed by the consumer, which are \r  typically self-performed, for an individual who lives in a private residence \r  and who, by reason of disability, is unable to perform such tasks but who is \r  capable of directing the appropriate performance of such tasks;</p>\r  \r   <p><s>32. </s><ins>33. </ins>Any practitioner of one of \r  the professions regulated by the Board of Medicine who is in good standing with \r  the applicable regulatory agency in another state from engaging in the practice \r  of that profession in Virginia with a patient who is being transported to or \r  from a Virginia hospital for care;</p>\r  \r   <p><s>33. </s><ins>34. </ins>Any doctor of medicine or \r  osteopathy, physician assistant, or advanced practice registered nurse who \r  would otherwise be subject to licensure by the Board who holds an active, \r  unrestricted license in another state, the District of Columbia, or a United \r  States territory or possession and who is in good standing with the applicable \r  regulatory agency in that state, the District of Columbia, or that United \r  States territory or possession who provides behavioral health services, as \r  defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/37.2-100\">37.2-100</a>, from engaging in the practice of his profession and \r  providing behavioral health services to a patient located in the Commonwealth \r  in accordance with the standard of care when (i) such practice is for the \r  purpose of providing continuity of care through the use of telemedicine \r  services as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/38.2-3418.16\">38.2-3418.16</a> and (ii) the practitioner has previously \r  established a practitioner-patient relationship with the patient and has \r  performed an in-person evaluation of the patient within the previous year. A \r  practitioner who provides behavioral health services to a patient located in \r  the Commonwealth through use of telemedicine services pursuant to this \r  subdivision may provide such services for a period of no more than one year \r  from the date on which the practitioner began providing such services to such \r  patient;</p>\r  \r   <p><s>34. </s><ins>35. </ins>Any employee of a program \r  licensed by the Department of Behavioral Health and Developmental Services who \r  is certified in cardiopulmonary resuscitation from acting in compliance with a \r  program participant\'s valid written order not to resuscitate issued in \r  accordance with § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2987.1\">54.1-2987.1</a> if such valid written order not to resuscitate is \r  included in the program participant\'s individualized service plan; or</p>\r  \r   <p><s>35. </s><ins>36. </ins>Any doctor of medicine or \r  osteopathy, physician assistant, respiratory therapist, occupational therapist, \r  or advanced practice registered nurse who would otherwise be subject to \r  licensure by the Board who holds an active, unrestricted license in another \r  state or the District of Columbia and who is in good standing with the \r  applicable regulatory agency in that state or the District of Columbia from \r  engaging in the practice of that profession in the Commonwealth with a patient \r  located in the Commonwealth when (i) such practice is for the purpose of \r  providing continuity of care through the use of telemedicine services as \r  defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/38.2-3418.16\">38.2-3418.16</a> and (ii) the patient is a current patient of the \r  practitioner with whom the practitioner has previously established a \r  practitioner-patient relationship and the practitioner has performed an \r  in-person examination of the patient within the previous 12 months. </p>\r  \r   <p>For purposes of this subdivision, if such practitioner with \r  whom the patient has previously established a practitioner-patient relationship \r  is unavailable at the time in which the patient seeks continuity of care, \r  another practitioner of the same subspecialty at the same practice group with \r  access to the patient\'s treatment history may provide continuity of care using \r  telemedicine services until the practitioner with whom the patient has a \r  previously established practitioner-patient relationship becomes available. For \r  the purposes of this subdivision, \"practitioner of the same \r  subspecialty\" means a practitioner who utilizes the same subspecialty \r  taxonomy code designation for claims processing. </p>\r  \r   <p>For the purposes of this subdivision, if a patient is (a) an \r  enrollee of a health maintenance organization that contracts with a \r  multispecialty group of practitioners, each of whom is licensed by the Board of \r  Medicine, and (b) a current patient of at least one practitioner who is a \r  member of the multispecialty group with whom such practitioner has previously \r  established a practitioner-patient relationship and of whom such practitioner \r  has performed an in-person examination within the previous 12 months, the \r  patient shall be deemed to be a current patient of each practitioner in the \r  multispecialty group with whom each such practitioner has established a \r  practitioner-patient relationship.</p>\r  \r   <p>B. Notwithstanding any provision of law or regulation to the \r  contrary, military medical personnel, as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/2.2-2001.4\">2.2-2001.4</a>, while \r  participating in a program established by the Department of Veterans Services \r  pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/2.2-2001.4\">2.2-2001.4</a>, may practice under the supervision of a licensed \r  physician or podiatrist or the chief medical officer of an organization \r  participating in such program, or his designee who is a licensee of the Board \r  and supervising within his scope of practice.</p>',NULL,0,'2024-01-10 23:55:03','2025-11-06 00:15:32'),
(1079552,74616,'HB1278ER',30,'2024-03-08','<br><center><b>VIRGINIA ACTS OF ASSEMBLY -- CHAPTER</b></center>\r \r <i>An Act to amend and reenact §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a> of the\r Code of Virginia, relating to auricular acupuncture; use of the five needle\r protocol.</i>\r \r <center>[H 1278]</center>\r \r <center>Approved</center>\r \r <p> </p>\r \r <p>Be it enacted by the General Assembly of Virginia:</p>\r \r <p>1. That §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a> of the Code of Virginia\r are amended and reenacted as follows:</p>\r \r <p>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a>. Definitions.</p>\r \r <p>As used in this chapter, unless the context requires a\r different meaning:</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Acupuncturist&quot; means an individual approved by the\r Board to practice acupuncture. This is limited to &quot;licensed\r acupuncturist&quot; which means an individual other than a doctor of medicine,\r osteopathy, chiropractic or podiatry who has successfully completed the\r requirements for licensure established by the Board (approved titles are\r limited to: Licensed Acupuncturist, Lic.Ac., and L.Ac.).</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Advanced practice registered nurse&quot; means a\r certified nurse midwife, certified registered nurse anesthetist, clinical nurse\r specialist, or nurse practitioner who is jointly licensed by the Boards of\r Medicine and Nursing pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>, has completed an advanced\r graduate-level education program in a specialty category of nursing, and has\r passed a national certifying examination for that specialty.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Auricular acupuncture&quot; means the subcutaneous\r insertion of sterile, disposable acupuncture needles in predetermined,\r bilateral locations in the outer ear<s> when used exclusively and specifically\r in the context of a chemical dependency treatment program</s>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Birth control&quot; means contraceptive methods that are\r approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. &quot;Birth control&quot;\r shall not be considered abortion for the purposes of Title 18.2.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Board&quot; means the Board of Medicine.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Certified nurse midwife&quot; means an advanced practice\r registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of nurse midwifery and who\r is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as an advanced\r practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Certified registered nurse anesthetist&quot; means an\r advanced practice registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of nurse\r anesthesia, who is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as an\r advanced practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>, and who practices\r under the supervision of a doctor of medicine, osteopathy, podiatry, or\r dentistry but is not subject to the practice agreement requirement described in\r § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Clinical nurse specialist&quot; means an advanced\r practice registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of clinical nurse\r specialist and who is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as\r an advanced practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Collaboration&quot; means the communication and\r decision-making process among health care providers who are members of a\r patient care team related to the treatment of a patient that includes the\r degree of cooperation necessary to provide treatment and care of the patient\r and includes (i) communication of data and information about the treatment and\r care of a patient, including the exchange of clinical observations and\r assessments, and (ii) development of an appropriate plan of care, including\r decisions regarding the health care provided, accessing and assessment of\r appropriate additional resources or expertise, and arrangement of appropriate\r referrals, testing, or studies.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Consultation&quot; means communicating data and\r information, exchanging clinical observations and assessments, accessing and\r assessing additional resources and expertise, problem-solving, and arranging\r for referrals, testing, or studies.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Genetic counselor&quot; means a person licensed by the\r Board to engage in the practice of genetic counseling.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Healing arts&quot; means the arts and sciences dealing\r with the prevention, diagnosis, treatment and cure or alleviation of human\r physical or mental ailments, conditions, diseases, pain or infirmities.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Licensed certified midwife&quot; means a person who is\r licensed as a certified midwife by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Medical malpractice judgment&quot; means any final order\r of any court entering judgment against a licensee of the Board that arises out\r of any tort action or breach of contract action for personal injuries or\r wrongful death, based on health care or professional services rendered, or that\r should have been rendered, by a health care provider, to a patient.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Medical malpractice settlement&quot; means any written\r agreement and release entered into by or on behalf of a licensee of the Board\r in response to a written claim for money damages that arises out of any\r personal injuries or wrongful death, based on health care or professional\r services rendered, or that should have been rendered, by a health care\r provider, to a patient.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Nurse practitioner&quot; means an advanced practice\r registered nurse, other than an advanced practice registered nurse licensed by\r the Boards of Medicine and Nursing in the category of certified nurse midwife,\r certified registered nurse anesthetist, or clinical nurse specialist, who is\r jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Occupational therapy assistant&quot; means an individual\r who has met the requirements of the Board for licensure and who works under the\r supervision of a licensed occupational therapist to assist in the practice of\r occupational therapy.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Patient care team&quot; means a multidisciplinary team\r of health care providers actively functioning as a unit with the management and\r leadership of one or more patient care team physicians for the purpose of\r providing and delivering health care to a patient or group of patients.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Patient care team physician&quot; means a physician who\r is actively licensed to practice medicine in the Commonwealth, who regularly\r practices medicine in the Commonwealth, and who provides management and\r leadership in the care of patients as part of a patient care team.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Patient care team podiatrist&quot; means a podiatrist\r who is actively licensed to practice podiatry in the Commonwealth, who\r regularly practices podiatry in the Commonwealth, and who provides management\r and leadership in the care of patients as part of a patient care team.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Physician assistant&quot; means a health care\r professional who has met the requirements of the Board for licensure as a\r physician assistant.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of acupuncture&quot; means the stimulation of\r certain points on or near the surface of the body by the insertion of needles\r to prevent or modify the perception of pain or to normalize physiological\r functions, including pain control, for the treatment of certain ailments or\r conditions of the body and includes the techniques of electroacupuncture,\r cupping<ins>,</ins> and moxibustion. The practice of acupuncture does not include\r the use of physical therapy, chiropractic, or osteopathic manipulative\r techniques; the use or prescribing of any drugs, medications, serums or\r vaccines; or the procedure of<ins> the five needle</ins> auricular acupuncture<ins>\r protocol (5NP)</ins> as exempted in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a><s> when used in the context of a\r chemical dependency treatment program for patients eligible for federal, state\r or local public funds by an employee of the program who is trained and approved\r by the National Acupuncture Detoxification Association or an equivalent\r certifying body</s>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of athletic training&quot; means the\r prevention, recognition, evaluation, and treatment of injuries or conditions\r related to athletic or recreational activity that requires physical skill and\r utilizes strength, power, endurance, speed, flexibility, range of motion or\r agility or a substantially similar injury or condition resulting from\r occupational activity immediately upon the onset of such injury or condition;\r and subsequent treatment and rehabilitation of such injuries or conditions under\r the direction of the patient\'s physician or under the direction of any doctor\r of medicine, osteopathy, chiropractic, podiatry, or dentistry, while using\r heat, light, sound, cold, electricity, exercise or mechanical or other devices.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of behavior analysis&quot; means the design,\r implementation, and evaluation of environmental modifications, using behavioral\r stimuli and consequences, to produce socially significant improvement in human\r behavior, including the use of direct observation, measurement, and functional\r analysis of the relationship between environment and behavior.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of chiropractic&quot; means the adjustment of\r the 24 movable vertebrae of the spinal column, and assisting nature for the\r purpose of normalizing the transmission of nerve energy, but does not include\r the use of surgery, obstetrics, osteopathy, or the administration or\r prescribing of any drugs, medicines, serums, or vaccines. &quot;Practice of\r chiropractic&quot;<s> shall include</s><ins> includes</ins> (i) requesting,\r receiving, and reviewing a patient\'s medical and physical history, including\r information related to past surgical and nonsurgical treatment of the patient\r and controlled substances prescribed to the patient, and (ii) documenting in a\r patient\'s record information related to the condition and symptoms of the\r patient, the examination and evaluation of the patient made by the doctor of\r chiropractic, and treatment provided to the patient by the doctor of\r chiropractic. &quot;Practice of chiropractic&quot;<s> shall</s> also<s> include</s><ins>\r includes</ins> performing the physical examination of an applicant for a\r commercial driver\'s license or commercial learner\'s permit pursuant to §\r <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/46.2-341.12\">46.2-341.12</a> if the practitioner has<s> (i)</s><ins> (a)</ins> applied for and\r received certification as a medical examiner pursuant to 49 C.F.R. Part 390,\r Subpart D and<s> (ii)</s><ins> (b)</ins> registered with the National Registry of\r Certified Medical Examiners.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of genetic counseling&quot; means (i) obtaining\r and evaluating individual and family medical histories to assess the risk of\r genetic medical conditions and diseases in a patient, his offspring, and other\r family members; (ii) discussing the features, history, diagnosis, environmental\r factors, and risk management of genetic medical conditions and diseases; (iii)\r ordering genetic laboratory tests and other diagnostic studies necessary for\r genetic assessment; (iv) integrating the results with personal and family\r medical history to assess and communicate risk factors for genetic medical\r conditions and diseases; (v) evaluating the patient\'s and family\'s responses to\r the medical condition or risk of recurrence and providing client-centered\r counseling and anticipatory guidance; (vi) identifying and utilizing community\r resources that provide medical, educational, financial, and psychosocial\r support and advocacy; and (vii) providing written documentation of medical,\r genetic, and counseling information for families and health care professionals.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of licensed certified midwifery&quot; means the\r provision of primary health care for preadolescents, adolescents, and adults\r within the scope of practice of a certified midwife established in accordance\r with the Standards for the Practice of Midwifery set by the American College of\r Nurse-Midwives, including (i) providing sexual and reproductive care and care\r during pregnancy and childbirth, postpartum care, and care for the newborn for\r up to 28 days following the birth of the child; (ii) prescribing of\r pharmacological and non-pharmacological therapies within the scope of the\r practice of midwifery; (iii) consulting or collaborating with or referring\r patients to such other health care providers as may be appropriate for the care\r of the patients; and (iv) serving as an educator in the theory and practice of\r midwifery.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of medicine or osteopathic medicine&quot; means\r the prevention, diagnosis, and treatment of human physical or mental ailments,\r conditions, diseases, pain, or infirmities by any means or method.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of occupational therapy&quot; means the\r therapeutic use of occupations for habilitation and rehabilitation to enhance\r physical health, mental health, and cognitive functioning and includes the\r evaluation, analysis, assessment, and delivery of education and training in\r basic and instrumental activities of daily living; the design, fabrication, and\r application of orthoses (splints); the design, selection, and use of adaptive\r equipment and assistive technologies; therapeutic activities to enhance\r functional performance; vocational evaluation and training; and consultation\r concerning the adaptation of physical, sensory, and social environments.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of podiatry&quot; means the prevention,\r diagnosis, treatment, and cure or alleviation of physical conditions, diseases,\r pain, or infirmities of the human foot and ankle, including the medical,\r mechanical and surgical treatment of the ailments of the human foot and ankle,\r but does not include amputation of the foot proximal to the transmetatarsal\r level through the metatarsal shafts. Amputations proximal to the\r metatarsal-phalangeal joints may only be performed in a hospital or ambulatory\r surgery facility accredited by an organization listed in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2939\">54.1-2939</a>. The\r practice includes the diagnosis and treatment of lower extremity ulcers;\r however, the treatment of severe lower extremity ulcers proximal to the foot\r and ankle may only be performed by appropriately trained, credentialed\r podiatrists in an approved hospital or ambulatory surgery center at which the\r podiatrist has privileges, as described in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2939\">54.1-2939</a>. The Board of Medicine\r shall determine whether a specific type of treatment of the foot and ankle is\r within the scope of practice of podiatry.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of radiologic technology&quot; means the\r application of ionizing radiation to human beings for diagnostic or therapeutic\r purposes.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of respiratory care&quot; means the (i)\r administration of pharmacological, diagnostic, and therapeutic agents related\r to respiratory care procedures necessary to implement a treatment, disease\r prevention, pulmonary rehabilitative, or diagnostic regimen prescribed by a\r practitioner of medicine or osteopathic medicine; (ii) transcription and\r implementation of the written or verbal orders of a practitioner of medicine or\r osteopathic medicine pertaining to the practice of respiratory care; (iii)\r observation and monitoring of signs and symptoms, general behavior, general\r physical response to respiratory care treatment and diagnostic testing,\r including determination of whether such signs, symptoms, reactions, behavior or\r general physical response exhibit abnormal characteristics; and (iv)\r implementation of respiratory care procedures, based on observed abnormalities,\r or appropriate reporting, referral, respiratory care protocols or changes in\r treatment pursuant to the written or verbal orders by a licensed practitioner\r of medicine or osteopathic medicine or the initiation of emergency procedures,\r pursuant to the Board\'s regulations or as otherwise authorized by law. The\r practice of respiratory care may be performed in any clinic, hospital, skilled\r nursing facility, private dwelling or other place deemed appropriate by the\r Board in accordance with the written or verbal order of a practitioner of\r medicine or osteopathic medicine<s>,</s> and shall be performed under qualified\r medical direction.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of surgical assisting&quot; means the\r performance of significant surgical tasks, including manipulation of organs,\r suturing of tissue, placement of hemostatic agents, injection of local\r anesthetic, harvesting of veins, implementation of devices, and other duties as\r directed by a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, or podiatry under the\r direct supervision of a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, or podiatry.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Qualified medical direction&quot; means, in the context\r of the practice of respiratory care, having readily accessible to the\r respiratory therapist a licensed practitioner of medicine or osteopathic\r medicine who has specialty training or experience in the management of acute\r and chronic respiratory disorders and who is responsible for the quality,\r safety, and appropriateness of the respiratory services provided by the\r respiratory therapist.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Radiologic technologist&quot; means an individual, other\r than a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, podiatry, or chiropractic or a\r dentist licensed pursuant to Chapter 27 (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2700\">54.1-2700</a> et seq.), who (i)\r performs, may be called upon to perform, or is licensed to perform a\r comprehensive scope of diagnostic or therapeutic radiologic procedures\r employing ionizing radiation and (ii) is delegated or exercises responsibility\r for the operation of radiation-generating equipment, the shielding of patient\r and staff from unnecessary radiation, the appropriate exposure of radiographs,\r the administration of radioactive chemical compounds under the direction of an\r authorized user as specified by regulations of the Department of Health, or\r other procedures that contribute to any significant extent to the site or\r dosage of ionizing radiation to which a patient is exposed.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Radiologic technologist, limited&quot; means an\r individual, other than a licensed radiologic technologist, dental hygienist, or\r person who is otherwise authorized by the Board of Dentistry under Chapter 27\r (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2700\">54.1-2700</a> et seq.) and the regulations pursuant thereto, who performs\r diagnostic radiographic procedures employing equipment that emits ionizing\r radiation that is limited to specific areas of the human body.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Radiologist assistant&quot; means an individual who has\r met the requirements of the Board for licensure as an advanced-level radiologic\r technologist and who, under the direct supervision of a licensed doctor of\r medicine or osteopathy specializing in the field of radiology, is authorized to\r (i) assess and evaluate the physiological and psychological responsiveness of\r patients undergoing radiologic procedures; (ii) evaluate image quality, make\r initial observations, and communicate observations to the supervising radiologist;\r (iii) administer contrast media or other medications prescribed by the\r supervising radiologist; and (iv) perform, or assist the supervising\r radiologist to perform, any other procedure consistent with the guidelines\r adopted by the American College of Radiology, the American Society of\r Radiologic Technologists, and the American Registry of Radiologic\r Technologists.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Respiratory care&quot; means the practice of the allied\r health profession responsible for the direct and indirect services, including\r inhalation therapy and respiratory therapy, in the treatment, management,\r diagnostic testing, control, and care of patients with deficiencies and\r abnormalities associated with the cardiopulmonary system under qualified\r medical direction.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Surgical assistant&quot; means an individual who has met\r the requirements of the Board for licensure as a surgical assistant and who\r works under the direct supervision of a licensed doctor of medicine,\r osteopathy, or podiatry.</p>\r \r <p>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a>. Exceptions and exemptions generally.</p>\r \r <p>A. The provisions of this chapter shall not prevent or\r prohibit:</p>\r \r <p>1. Any person entitled to practice his profession under any\r prior law on June 24, 1944, from continuing such practice within the scope of\r the definition of his particular school of practice;</p>\r \r <p>2. Any person licensed to practice naturopathy prior to June\r 30, 1980, from continuing such practice in accordance with regulations\r promulgated by the Board;</p>\r \r <p>3. Any licensed advanced practice registered nurse from\r rendering care in accordance with the provisions of §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a> and\r <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957.01\">54.1-2957.01</a>, any advanced practice registered nurse licensed by the Boards of\r Medicine and Nursing in the category of certified nurse midwife practicing\r pursuant to subsection H of § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>, or any advanced practice registered\r nurse licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing in the category of\r clinical nurse specialist practicing pursuant to subsection J of § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>\r when such services are authorized by regulations promulgated jointly by the\r Boards of Medicine and Nursing;</p>\r \r <p>4. Any registered professional nurse, licensed advanced\r practice registered nurse, graduate laboratory technician<ins>,</ins> or other\r technical personnel who have been properly trained from rendering care or\r services within the scope of their usual professional activities which shall\r include the taking of blood, the giving of intravenous infusions and\r intravenous injections, and the insertion of tubes when performed under the\r orders of a person licensed to practice medicine or osteopathy, an advanced\r practice registered nurse, or a physician assistant;</p>\r \r <p>5. Any dentist, pharmacist<ins>,</ins> or optometrist from rendering\r care or services within the scope of his usual professional activities;</p>\r \r <p>6. Any practitioner licensed or certified by the Board from\r delegating to personnel supervised by him, such activities or functions as are\r nondiscretionary and do not require the exercise of professional judgment for\r their performance and which are usually or customarily delegated to such\r persons by practitioners of the healing arts, if such activities or functions\r are authorized by and performed for such practitioners of the healing arts and\r responsibility for such activities or functions is assumed by such\r practitioners of the healing arts;</p>\r \r <p>7. The rendering of medical advice or information through\r telecommunications from a physician licensed to practice medicine in Virginia\r or an adjoining state, or from a licensed advanced practice registered nurse,\r to emergency medical personnel acting in an emergency situation;</p>\r \r <p>8. The domestic administration of family remedies;</p>\r \r <p>9. The giving or use of massages, steam baths, dry heat rooms,\r infrared heat<ins>,</ins> or ultraviolet lamps in public or private health clubs\r and spas;</p>\r \r <p>10. The manufacture or sale of proprietary medicines in this\r Commonwealth by licensed pharmacists or druggists;</p>\r \r <p>11. The advertising or sale of commercial appliances or\r remedies;</p>\r \r <p>12. The fitting by nonitinerant persons or manufacturers of\r artificial eyes, limbs or other apparatus or appliances or the fitting of\r plaster cast counterparts of deformed portions of the body by a nonitinerant\r bracemaker or prosthetist for the purpose of having a three-dimensional record\r of the deformity, when such bracemaker or prosthetist has received a\r prescription from a licensed physician, licensed advanced practice registered\r nurse, or licensed physician assistant directing the fitting of such casts and\r such activities are conducted in conformity with the laws of Virginia;</p>\r \r <p>13. Any person from the rendering of first aid or medical\r assistance in an emergency in the absence of a person licensed to practice\r medicine or osteopathy under the provisions of this chapter;</p>\r \r <p>14. The practice of the religious tenets of any church in the\r ministration to the sick and suffering by mental or spiritual means without the\r use of any drug or material remedy, whether gratuitously or for compensation;</p>\r \r <p>15. Any legally qualified out-of-state or foreign practitioner\r from meeting in consultation with legally licensed practitioners in this\r Commonwealth;</p>\r \r <p>16. Any practitioner of the healing arts licensed or certified\r and in good standing with the applicable regulatory agency in another state or\r Canada when that practitioner of the healing arts is in Virginia temporarily\r and such practitioner has been issued a temporary authorization by the Board\r from practicing medicine or the duties of the profession for which he is\r licensed or certified (i) in a summer camp or in conjunction with patients who\r are participating in recreational activities, (ii) while participating in\r continuing educational programs prescribed by the Board, or (iii) by rendering\r at any site any health care services within the limits of his license,\r voluntarily and without compensation, to any patient of any clinic which is\r organized in whole or in part for the delivery of health care services without\r charge as provided in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-106\">54.1-106</a>;</p>\r \r <p>17. The performance of the duties of any active duty health\r care provider in active service in the army, navy, coast guard, marine corps,\r air force, or public health service of the United States at any public or\r private health care facility while such individual is so commissioned or\r serving and in accordance with his official military duties;</p>\r \r <p>18. Any masseur, who publicly represents himself as such, from\r performing services within the scope of his usual professional activities and\r in conformance with state law;</p>\r \r <p>19. Any person from performing services in the lawful conduct\r of his particular profession or business under state law;</p>\r \r <p>20. Any person from rendering emergency care pursuant to the\r provisions of § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/8.01-225\">8.01-225</a>;</p>\r \r <p>21. Qualified emergency medical services personnel, when\r acting within the scope of their certification, and licensed health care\r practitioners, when acting within their scope of practice, from following\r Durable Do Not Resuscitate Orders issued in accordance with § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2987.1\">54.1-2987.1</a> and\r Board of Health regulations, or licensed health care practitioners from\r following any other written order of a physician not to resuscitate a patient\r in the event of cardiac or respiratory arrest;</p>\r \r <p>22. Any commissioned or contract medical officer of the army,\r navy, coast guard or air force rendering services voluntarily and without\r compensation while deemed to be licensed pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-106\">54.1-106</a>;</p>\r \r <p>23. Any<s> provider of a chemical dependency treatment program\r who is certified as an &quot;acupuncture detoxification specialist&quot; by the\r National Acupuncture Detoxification Association or an equivalent certifying\r body, from administering auricular acupuncture treatment under the appropriate\r supervision of a National Acupuncture Detoxification Association certified\r licensed physician or licensed acupuncturist</s><ins> person from engaging in the\r five needle auricular acupuncture protocol (5NP), a standardized five needle protocol\r wherein up to five needles are inserted into the external human ear to provide\r relief from the effects of behavioral health conditions, provided such person\r (i) has appropriate training in the 5NP, including training established by the\r National Acupuncture Detoxification Association or equivalent certifying body;\r (ii) does not use any letters, words, or insignia indicating or implying that\r the person is an acupuncturist; and (iii) makes no statements implying that his\r practice of the 5NP is licensed, certified, or otherwise overseen by the\r Commonwealth. Treatment utilizing the 5NP pursuant to this subdivision shall be\r strictly limited to the insertion of disposable sterile acupuncture needles\r into the ear and only in compliance with the 5NP. The application or insertion\r of needles anywhere else on the body of another person by a person acting under\r the provisions of this subdivision shall be considered engaging in the practice\r of acupuncture without a license</ins>;</p>\r \r <p>24. Any employee of any assisted living facility who is\r certified in cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) acting in compliance with the\r patient\'s individualized service plan and with the written order of the\r attending physician not to resuscitate a patient in the event of cardiac or\r respiratory arrest;</p>\r \r <p>25. Any person working as a health assistant under the\r direction of a licensed medical or osteopathic doctor within the Department of\r Corrections, the Department of Juvenile Justice or local correctional\r facilities;</p>\r \r <p>26. Any employee of a school board, authorized by a prescriber\r and trained in the administration of insulin and glucagon, when, upon the\r authorization of a prescriber and the written request of the parents as defined\r in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/22.1-1\">22.1-1</a>, assisting with the administration of insulin or administrating\r glucagon to a student diagnosed as having diabetes and who requires insulin\r injections during the school day or for whom glucagon has been prescribed for\r the emergency treatment of hypoglycemia;</p>\r \r <p>27. Any practitioner of the healing arts or other profession\r regulated by the Board from rendering free health care to an underserved\r population of Virginia who (i) does not regularly practice his profession in\r Virginia, (ii) holds a current valid license or certificate to practice his\r profession in another state, territory, district or possession of the United\r States, (iii) volunteers to provide free health care to an underserved area of\r the Commonwealth under the auspices of a publicly supported all volunteer,\r nonprofit organization that sponsors the provision of health care to\r populations of underserved people, (iv) files a copy of the license or\r certification issued in such other jurisdiction with the Board, (v) notifies\r the Board at least five business days prior to the voluntary provision of\r services of the dates and location of such service, and (vi) acknowledges, in\r writing, that such licensure exemption shall only be valid, in compliance with\r the Board\'s regulations, during the limited period that such free health care\r is made available through the volunteer, nonprofit organization on the dates\r and at the location filed with the Board. The Board may deny the right to\r practice in Virginia to any practitioner of the healing arts whose license or\r certificate has been previously suspended or revoked, who has been convicted of\r a felony or who is otherwise found to be in violation of applicable laws or\r regulations. However, the Board shall allow a practitioner of the healing arts\r who meets the above criteria to provide volunteer services without prior notice\r for a period of up to three days, provided the nonprofit organization verifies\r that the practitioner has a valid, unrestricted license in another state;</p>\r \r <p>28. Any registered nurse, acting as an agent of the Department\r of Health, from obtaining specimens of sputum or other bodily fluid from\r persons in whom the diagnosis of active tuberculosis disease, as defined in §\r <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-49.1\">32.1-49.1</a>, is suspected and submitting orders for testing of such specimens to\r the Division of Consolidated Laboratories or other public health laboratories,\r designated by the State Health Commissioner, for the purpose of determining the\r presence or absence of tubercle bacilli as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-49.1\">32.1-49.1</a>;</p>\r \r <p>29. Any physician of medicine or osteopathy or advanced\r practice registered nurse from delegating to a registered nurse under his\r supervision the screening and testing of children for elevated blood-lead\r levels when such testing is conducted (i) in accordance with a written protocol\r between the physician or advanced practice registered nurse and the registered\r nurse and (ii) in compliance with the Board of Health\'s regulations promulgated\r pursuant to §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-46.1\">32.1-46.1</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-46.2\">32.1-46.2</a>. Any follow-up testing or treatment\r shall be conducted at the direction of a physician or an advanced practice\r registered nurse;</p>\r \r <p>30. Any practitioner of one of the professions regulated by\r the Board of Medicine who is in good standing with the applicable regulatory\r agency in another state or Canada from engaging in the practice of that\r profession when the practitioner is in Virginia temporarily with an\r out-of-state athletic team or athlete for the duration of the athletic\r tournament, game, or event in which the team or athlete is competing;</p>\r \r <p>31. Any person from performing state or federally funded\r health care tasks directed by the consumer, which are typically self-performed,\r for an individual who lives in a private residence and who, by reason of\r disability, is unable to perform such tasks but who is capable of directing the\r appropriate performance of such tasks;</p>\r \r <p>32. Any practitioner of one of the professions regulated by\r the Board of Medicine who is in good standing with the applicable regulatory\r agency in another state from engaging in the practice of that profession in\r Virginia with a patient who is being transported to or from a Virginia hospital\r for care;</p>\r \r <p>33. Any doctor of medicine or osteopathy, physician assistant,\r or advanced practice registered nurse who would otherwise be subject to\r licensure by the Board who holds an active, unrestricted license in another\r state, the District of Columbia, or a United States territory or possession and\r who is in good standing with the applicable regulatory agency in that state,\r the District of Columbia, or that United States territory or possession who\r provides behavioral health services, as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/37.2-100\">37.2-100</a>, from engaging in\r the practice of his profession and providing behavioral health services to a\r patient located in the Commonwealth in accordance with the standard of care\r when (i) such practice is for the purpose of providing continuity of care\r through the use of telemedicine services as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/38.2-3418.16\">38.2-3418.16</a> and (ii)\r the practitioner has previously established a practitioner-patient relationship\r with the patient and has performed an in-person evaluation of the patient\r within the previous year. A practitioner who provides behavioral health\r services to a patient located in the Commonwealth through use of telemedicine\r services pursuant to this subdivision may provide such services for a period of\r no more than one year from the date on which the practitioner began providing\r such services to such patient;</p>\r \r <p>34. Any employee of a program licensed by the Department of\r Behavioral Health and Developmental Services who is certified in\r cardiopulmonary resuscitation from acting in compliance with a program\r participant\'s valid written order not to resuscitate issued in accordance with\r § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2987.1\">54.1-2987.1</a> if such valid written order not to resuscitate is included in the\r program participant\'s individualized service plan; or</p>\r \r <p>35. Any doctor of medicine or osteopathy, physician assistant,\r respiratory therapist, occupational therapist, or advanced practice registered\r nurse who would otherwise be subject to licensure by the Board who holds an\r active, unrestricted license in another state or the District of Columbia and\r who is in good standing with the applicable regulatory agency in that state or\r the District of Columbia from engaging in the practice of that profession in\r the Commonwealth with a patient located in the Commonwealth when (i) such\r practice is for the purpose of providing continuity of care through the use of\r telemedicine services as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/38.2-3418.16\">38.2-3418.16</a> and (ii) the patient is a\r current patient of the practitioner with whom the practitioner has previously\r established a practitioner-patient relationship and the practitioner has\r performed an in-person examination of the patient within the previous 12\r months. </p>\r \r <p>For purposes of this subdivision, if such practitioner with\r whom the patient has previously established a practitioner-patient relationship\r is unavailable at the time in which the patient seeks continuity of care,\r another practitioner of the same subspecialty at the same practice group with\r access to the patient\'s treatment history may provide continuity of care using\r telemedicine services until the practitioner with whom the patient has a\r previously established practitioner-patient relationship becomes available. For\r the purposes of this subdivision, &quot;practitioner of the same\r subspecialty&quot; means a practitioner who utilizes the same subspecialty\r taxonomy code designation for claims processing. </p>\r \r <p>For the purposes of this subdivision, if a patient is (a) an\r enrollee of a health maintenance organization that contracts with a\r multispecialty group of practitioners, each of whom is licensed by the Board of\r Medicine, and (b) a current patient of at least one practitioner who is a\r member of the multispecialty group with whom such practitioner has previously\r established a practitioner-patient relationship and of whom such practitioner\r has performed an in-person examination within the previous 12 months, the\r patient shall be deemed to be a current patient of each practitioner in the\r multispecialty group with whom each such practitioner has established a\r practitioner-patient relationship.</p>\r \r <p>B. Notwithstanding any provision of law or regulation to the\r contrary, military medical personnel, as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/2.2-2001.4\">2.2-2001.4</a>, while\r participating in a program established by the Department of Veterans Services\r pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/2.2-2001.4\">2.2-2001.4</a>, may practice under the supervision of a licensed\r physician or podiatrist or the chief medical officer of an organization\r participating in such program, or his designee who is a licensee of the Board\r and supervising within his scope of practice.</p>',NULL,0,'2024-03-08 14:55:02','2025-11-06 00:15:32'),
(1045567,74616,'HB1278H1',30,'2024-02-06','<br><center><b>HOUSE BILL NO. 1278</b></center>\r \r <center>AMENDMENT IN THE NATURE OF A SUBSTITUTE</center>\r \r <center>(Proposed by the House Committee on Health and Human Services</center>\r \r <center>on February 6, 2024)</center>\r \r <center>(Patron Prior to Substitute--Delegate Zehr)</center>\r \r <i>A BILL to amend and reenact §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a> of the Code\r of Virginia, relating to auricular acupuncture; use of the five needle\r protocol.</i>\r \r <p>Be it enacted by the General Assembly of Virginia:</p>\r \r <p>1. That §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a> of the Code of Virginia\r are amended and reenacted as follows:</p>\r \r <p>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2900\">54.1-2900</a>. Definitions.</p>\r \r <p>As used in this chapter, unless the context requires a\r different meaning:</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Acupuncturist&quot; means an individual approved by the\r Board to practice acupuncture. This is limited to &quot;licensed\r acupuncturist&quot; which means an individual other than a doctor of medicine,\r osteopathy, chiropractic or podiatry who has successfully completed the\r requirements for licensure established by the Board (approved titles are\r limited to: Licensed Acupuncturist, Lic.Ac., and L.Ac.).</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Advanced practice registered nurse&quot; means a certified\r nurse midwife, certified registered nurse anesthetist, clinical nurse\r specialist, or nurse practitioner who is jointly licensed by the Boards of\r Medicine and Nursing pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>, has completed an advanced\r graduate-level education program in a specialty category of nursing, and has\r passed a national certifying examination for that specialty.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Auricular acupuncture&quot; means the subcutaneous\r insertion of sterile, disposable acupuncture needles in predetermined,\r bilateral locations in the outer ear<s> when used exclusively and specifically\r in the context of a chemical dependency treatment program</s>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Birth control&quot; means contraceptive methods that are\r approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration. &quot;Birth control&quot;\r shall not be considered abortion for the purposes of Title 18.2.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Board&quot; means the Board of Medicine.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Certified nurse midwife&quot; means an advanced practice\r registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of nurse midwifery and who\r is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as an advanced\r practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Certified registered nurse anesthetist&quot; means an\r advanced practice registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of nurse\r anesthesia, who is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as an\r advanced practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>, and who practices\r under the supervision of a doctor of medicine, osteopathy, podiatry, or\r dentistry but is not subject to the practice agreement requirement described in\r § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Clinical nurse specialist&quot; means an advanced\r practice registered nurse who is certified in the specialty of clinical nurse\r specialist and who is jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing as\r an advanced practice registered nurse pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Collaboration&quot; means the communication and\r decision-making process among health care providers who are members of a\r patient care team related to the treatment of a patient that includes the\r degree of cooperation necessary to provide treatment and care of the patient\r and includes (i) communication of data and information about the treatment and\r care of a patient, including the exchange of clinical observations and\r assessments, and (ii) development of an appropriate plan of care, including\r decisions regarding the health care provided, accessing and assessment of\r appropriate additional resources or expertise, and arrangement of appropriate\r referrals, testing, or studies.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Consultation&quot; means communicating data and\r information, exchanging clinical observations and assessments, accessing and\r assessing additional resources and expertise, problem-solving, and arranging\r for referrals, testing, or studies.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Genetic counselor&quot; means a person licensed by the\r Board to engage in the practice of genetic counseling.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Healing arts&quot; means the arts and sciences dealing\r with the prevention, diagnosis, treatment and cure or alleviation of human\r physical or mental ailments, conditions, diseases, pain or infirmities.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Licensed certified midwife&quot; means a person who is\r licensed as a certified midwife by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Medical malpractice judgment&quot; means any final order\r of any court entering judgment against a licensee of the Board that arises out\r of any tort action or breach of contract action for personal injuries or\r wrongful death, based on health care or professional services rendered, or that\r should have been rendered, by a health care provider, to a patient.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Medical malpractice settlement&quot; means any written agreement\r and release entered into by or on behalf of a licensee of the Board in response\r to a written claim for money damages that arises out of any personal injuries\r or wrongful death, based on health care or professional services rendered, or\r that should have been rendered, by a health care provider, to a patient.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Nurse practitioner&quot; means an advanced practice\r registered nurse, other than an advanced practice registered nurse licensed by\r the Boards of Medicine and Nursing in the category of certified nurse midwife,\r certified registered nurse anesthetist, or clinical nurse specialist, who is\r jointly licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Occupational therapy assistant&quot; means an individual\r who has met the requirements of the Board for licensure and who works under the\r supervision of a licensed occupational therapist to assist in the practice of\r occupational therapy.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Patient care team&quot; means a multidisciplinary team\r of health care providers actively functioning as a unit with the management and\r leadership of one or more patient care team physicians for the purpose of\r providing and delivering health care to a patient or group of patients.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Patient care team physician&quot; means a physician who\r is actively licensed to practice medicine in the Commonwealth, who regularly\r practices medicine in the Commonwealth, and who provides management and\r leadership in the care of patients as part of a patient care team.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Patient care team podiatrist&quot; means a podiatrist\r who is actively licensed to practice podiatry in the Commonwealth, who\r regularly practices podiatry in the Commonwealth, and who provides management\r and leadership in the care of patients as part of a patient care team.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Physician assistant&quot; means a health care\r professional who has met the requirements of the Board for licensure as a\r physician assistant.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of acupuncture&quot; means the stimulation of\r certain points on or near the surface of the body by the insertion of needles\r to prevent or modify the perception of pain or to normalize physiological\r functions, including pain control, for the treatment of certain ailments or\r conditions of the body and includes the techniques of electroacupuncture,\r cupping<ins>,</ins> and moxibustion. The practice of acupuncture does not include\r the use of physical therapy, chiropractic, or osteopathic manipulative\r techniques; the use or prescribing of any drugs, medications, serums or\r vaccines; or the procedure of<ins> the five needle</ins> auricular acupuncture<ins>\r protocol (5NP)</ins> as exempted in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a><s> when used in the context of a\r chemical dependency treatment program for patients eligible for federal, state\r or local public funds by an employee of the program who is trained and approved\r by the National Acupuncture Detoxification Association or an equivalent\r certifying body</s>.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of athletic training&quot; means the\r prevention, recognition, evaluation, and treatment of injuries or conditions\r related to athletic or recreational activity that requires physical skill and\r utilizes strength, power, endurance, speed, flexibility, range of motion or\r agility or a substantially similar injury or condition resulting from\r occupational activity immediately upon the onset of such injury or condition;\r and subsequent treatment and rehabilitation of such injuries or conditions\r under the direction of the patient\'s physician or under the direction of any\r doctor of medicine, osteopathy, chiropractic, podiatry, or dentistry, while\r using heat, light, sound, cold, electricity, exercise or mechanical or other\r devices.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of behavior analysis&quot; means the design,\r implementation, and evaluation of environmental modifications, using behavioral\r stimuli and consequences, to produce socially significant improvement in human\r behavior, including the use of direct observation, measurement, and functional\r analysis of the relationship between environment and behavior.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of chiropractic&quot; means the adjustment of\r the 24 movable vertebrae of the spinal column, and assisting nature for the\r purpose of normalizing the transmission of nerve energy, but does not include\r the use of surgery, obstetrics, osteopathy, or the administration or\r prescribing of any drugs, medicines, serums, or vaccines. &quot;Practice of\r chiropractic&quot;<s> shall include</s><ins> includes</ins> (i) requesting,\r receiving, and reviewing a patient\'s medical and physical history, including\r information related to past surgical and nonsurgical treatment of the patient\r and controlled substances prescribed to the patient, and (ii) documenting in a\r patient\'s record information related to the condition and symptoms of the\r patient, the examination and evaluation of the patient made by the doctor of\r chiropractic, and treatment provided to the patient by the doctor of\r chiropractic. &quot;Practice of chiropractic&quot;<s> shall</s> also<s> include</s><ins>\r includes</ins> performing the physical examination of an applicant for a\r commercial driver\'s license or commercial learner\'s permit pursuant to §\r <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/46.2-341.12\">46.2-341.12</a> if the practitioner has<s> (i)</s><ins> (a)</ins> applied for and\r received certification as a medical examiner pursuant to 49 C.F.R. Part 390,\r Subpart D and<s> (ii)</s><ins> (b)</ins> registered with the National Registry of\r Certified Medical Examiners.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of genetic counseling&quot; means (i) obtaining\r and evaluating individual and family medical histories to assess the risk of\r genetic medical conditions and diseases in a patient, his offspring, and other\r family members; (ii) discussing the features, history, diagnosis, environmental\r factors, and risk management of genetic medical conditions and diseases; (iii)\r ordering genetic laboratory tests and other diagnostic studies necessary for\r genetic assessment; (iv) integrating the results with personal and family\r medical history to assess and communicate risk factors for genetic medical\r conditions and diseases; (v) evaluating the patient\'s and family\'s responses to\r the medical condition or risk of recurrence and providing client-centered\r counseling and anticipatory guidance; (vi) identifying and utilizing community\r resources that provide medical, educational, financial, and psychosocial\r support and advocacy; and (vii) providing written documentation of medical,\r genetic, and counseling information for families and health care professionals.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of licensed certified midwifery&quot; means the\r provision of primary health care for preadolescents, adolescents, and adults\r within the scope of practice of a certified midwife established in accordance\r with the Standards for the Practice of Midwifery set by the American College of\r Nurse-Midwives, including (i) providing sexual and reproductive care and care\r during pregnancy and childbirth, postpartum care, and care for the newborn for\r up to 28 days following the birth of the child; (ii) prescribing of\r pharmacological and non-pharmacological therapies within the scope of the\r practice of midwifery; (iii) consulting or collaborating with or referring patients\r to such other health care providers as may be appropriate for the care of the\r patients; and (iv) serving as an educator in the theory and practice of\r midwifery.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of medicine or osteopathic medicine&quot; means\r the prevention, diagnosis, and treatment of human physical or mental ailments,\r conditions, diseases, pain, or infirmities by any means or method.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of occupational therapy&quot; means the\r therapeutic use of occupations for habilitation and rehabilitation to enhance\r physical health, mental health, and cognitive functioning and includes the\r evaluation, analysis, assessment, and delivery of education and training in\r basic and instrumental activities of daily living; the design, fabrication, and\r application of orthoses (splints); the design, selection, and use of adaptive\r equipment and assistive technologies; therapeutic activities to enhance\r functional performance; vocational evaluation and training; and consultation\r concerning the adaptation of physical, sensory, and social environments.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of podiatry&quot; means the prevention,\r diagnosis, treatment, and cure or alleviation of physical conditions, diseases,\r pain, or infirmities of the human foot and ankle, including the medical,\r mechanical and surgical treatment of the ailments of the human foot and ankle,\r but does not include amputation of the foot proximal to the transmetatarsal\r level through the metatarsal shafts. Amputations proximal to the\r metatarsal-phalangeal joints may only be performed in a hospital or ambulatory\r surgery facility accredited by an organization listed in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2939\">54.1-2939</a>. The\r practice includes the diagnosis and treatment of lower extremity ulcers;\r however, the treatment of severe lower extremity ulcers proximal to the foot\r and ankle may only be performed by appropriately trained, credentialed\r podiatrists in an approved hospital or ambulatory surgery center at which the\r podiatrist has privileges, as described in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2939\">54.1-2939</a>. The Board of Medicine\r shall determine whether a specific type of treatment of the foot and ankle is within\r the scope of practice of podiatry.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of radiologic technology&quot; means the\r application of ionizing radiation to human beings for diagnostic or therapeutic\r purposes.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of respiratory care&quot; means the (i)\r administration of pharmacological, diagnostic, and therapeutic agents related\r to respiratory care procedures necessary to implement a treatment, disease\r prevention, pulmonary rehabilitative, or diagnostic regimen prescribed by a\r practitioner of medicine or osteopathic medicine; (ii) transcription and\r implementation of the written or verbal orders of a practitioner of medicine or\r osteopathic medicine pertaining to the practice of respiratory care; (iii)\r observation and monitoring of signs and symptoms, general behavior, general\r physical response to respiratory care treatment and diagnostic testing,\r including determination of whether such signs, symptoms, reactions, behavior or\r general physical response exhibit abnormal characteristics; and (iv)\r implementation of respiratory care procedures, based on observed abnormalities,\r or appropriate reporting, referral, respiratory care protocols or changes in\r treatment pursuant to the written or verbal orders by a licensed practitioner\r of medicine or osteopathic medicine or the initiation of emergency procedures,\r pursuant to the Board\'s regulations or as otherwise authorized by law. The\r practice of respiratory care may be performed in any clinic, hospital, skilled\r nursing facility, private dwelling or other place deemed appropriate by the\r Board in accordance with the written or verbal order of a practitioner of\r medicine or osteopathic medicine<s>,</s> and shall be performed under qualified\r medical direction.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Practice of surgical assisting&quot; means the\r performance of significant surgical tasks, including manipulation of organs,\r suturing of tissue, placement of hemostatic agents, injection of local\r anesthetic, harvesting of veins, implementation of devices, and other duties as\r directed by a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, or podiatry under the\r direct supervision of a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, or podiatry.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Qualified medical direction&quot; means, in the context\r of the practice of respiratory care, having readily accessible to the\r respiratory therapist a licensed practitioner of medicine or osteopathic\r medicine who has specialty training or experience in the management of acute\r and chronic respiratory disorders and who is responsible for the quality,\r safety, and appropriateness of the respiratory services provided by the\r respiratory therapist.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Radiologic technologist&quot; means an individual, other\r than a licensed doctor of medicine, osteopathy, podiatry, or chiropractic or a\r dentist licensed pursuant to Chapter 27 (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2700\">54.1-2700</a> et seq.), who (i)\r performs, may be called upon to perform, or is licensed to perform a\r comprehensive scope of diagnostic or therapeutic radiologic procedures\r employing ionizing radiation and (ii) is delegated or exercises responsibility\r for the operation of radiation-generating equipment, the shielding of patient\r and staff from unnecessary radiation, the appropriate exposure of radiographs,\r the administration of radioactive chemical compounds under the direction of an\r authorized user as specified by regulations of the Department of Health, or\r other procedures that contribute to any significant extent to the site or\r dosage of ionizing radiation to which a patient is exposed.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Radiologic technologist, limited&quot; means an\r individual, other than a licensed radiologic technologist, dental hygienist, or\r person who is otherwise authorized by the Board of Dentistry under Chapter 27\r (§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2700\">54.1-2700</a> et seq.) and the regulations pursuant thereto, who performs\r diagnostic radiographic procedures employing equipment that emits ionizing\r radiation that is limited to specific areas of the human body.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Radiologist assistant&quot; means an individual who has\r met the requirements of the Board for licensure as an advanced-level radiologic\r technologist and who, under the direct supervision of a licensed doctor of\r medicine or osteopathy specializing in the field of radiology, is authorized to\r (i) assess and evaluate the physiological and psychological responsiveness of\r patients undergoing radiologic procedures; (ii) evaluate image quality, make\r initial observations, and communicate observations to the supervising radiologist;\r (iii) administer contrast media or other medications prescribed by the\r supervising radiologist; and (iv) perform, or assist the supervising\r radiologist to perform, any other procedure consistent with the guidelines\r adopted by the American College of Radiology, the American Society of\r Radiologic Technologists, and the American Registry of Radiologic\r Technologists.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Respiratory care&quot; means the practice of the allied\r health profession responsible for the direct and indirect services, including\r inhalation therapy and respiratory therapy, in the treatment, management,\r diagnostic testing, control, and care of patients with deficiencies and\r abnormalities associated with the cardiopulmonary system under qualified\r medical direction.</p>\r \r <p>&quot;Surgical assistant&quot; means an individual who has met\r the requirements of the Board for licensure as a surgical assistant and who\r works under the direct supervision of a licensed doctor of medicine,\r osteopathy, or podiatry.</p>\r \r <p>§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2901\">54.1-2901</a>. Exceptions and exemptions generally.</p>\r \r <p>A. The provisions of this chapter shall not prevent or\r prohibit:</p>\r \r <p>1. Any person entitled to practice his profession under any\r prior law on June 24, 1944, from continuing such practice within the scope of\r the definition of his particular school of practice;</p>\r \r <p>2. Any person licensed to practice naturopathy prior to June\r 30, 1980, from continuing such practice in accordance with regulations\r promulgated by the Board;</p>\r \r <p>3. Any licensed advanced practice registered nurse from\r rendering care in accordance with the provisions of §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a> and\r <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957.01\">54.1-2957.01</a>, any advanced practice registered nurse licensed by the Boards of\r Medicine and Nursing in the category of certified nurse midwife practicing\r pursuant to subsection H of § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>, or any advanced practice registered\r nurse licensed by the Boards of Medicine and Nursing in the category of\r clinical nurse specialist practicing pursuant to subsection J of § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2957\">54.1-2957</a>\r when such services are authorized by regulations promulgated jointly by the\r Boards of Medicine and Nursing;</p>\r \r <p>4. Any registered professional nurse, licensed advanced\r practice registered nurse, graduate laboratory technician<ins>,</ins> or other\r technical personnel who have been properly trained from rendering care or\r services within the scope of their usual professional activities which shall\r include the taking of blood, the giving of intravenous infusions and\r intravenous injections, and the insertion of tubes when performed under the\r orders of a person licensed to practice medicine or osteopathy, an advanced\r practice registered nurse, or a physician assistant;</p>\r \r <p>5. Any dentist, pharmacist<ins>,</ins> or optometrist from\r rendering care or services within the scope of his usual professional\r activities;</p>\r \r <p>6. Any practitioner licensed or certified by the Board from\r delegating to personnel supervised by him, such activities or functions as are\r nondiscretionary and do not require the exercise of professional judgment for\r their performance and which are usually or customarily delegated to such\r persons by practitioners of the healing arts, if such activities or functions\r are authorized by and performed for such practitioners of the healing arts and\r responsibility for such activities or functions is assumed by such\r practitioners of the healing arts;</p>\r \r <p>7. The rendering of medical advice or information through\r telecommunications from a physician licensed to practice medicine in Virginia\r or an adjoining state, or from a licensed advanced practice registered nurse,\r to emergency medical personnel acting in an emergency situation;</p>\r \r <p>8. The domestic administration of family remedies;</p>\r \r <p>9. The giving or use of massages, steam baths, dry heat rooms,\r infrared heat<ins>,</ins> or ultraviolet lamps in public or private health clubs\r and spas;</p>\r \r <p>10. The manufacture or sale of proprietary medicines in this\r Commonwealth by licensed pharmacists or druggists;</p>\r \r <p>11. The advertising or sale of commercial appliances or\r remedies;</p>\r \r <p>12. The fitting by nonitinerant persons or manufacturers of\r artificial eyes, limbs or other apparatus or appliances or the fitting of plaster\r cast counterparts of deformed portions of the body by a nonitinerant bracemaker\r or prosthetist for the purpose of having a three-dimensional record of the\r deformity, when such bracemaker or prosthetist has received a prescription from\r a licensed physician, licensed advanced practice registered nurse, or licensed\r physician assistant directing the fitting of such casts and such activities are\r conducted in conformity with the laws of Virginia;</p>\r \r <p>13. Any person from the rendering of first aid or medical assistance\r in an emergency in the absence of a person licensed to practice medicine or\r osteopathy under the provisions of this chapter;</p>\r \r <p>14. The practice of the religious tenets of any church in the\r ministration to the sick and suffering by mental or spiritual means without the\r use of any drug or material remedy, whether gratuitously or for compensation;</p>\r \r <p>15. Any legally qualified out-of-state or foreign practitioner\r from meeting in consultation with legally licensed practitioners in this\r Commonwealth;</p>\r \r <p>16. Any practitioner of the healing arts licensed or certified\r and in good standing with the applicable regulatory agency in another state or\r Canada when that practitioner of the healing arts is in Virginia temporarily\r and such practitioner has been issued a temporary authorization by the Board\r from practicing medicine or the duties of the profession for which he is\r licensed or certified (i) in a summer camp or in conjunction with patients who\r are participating in recreational activities, (ii) while participating in\r continuing educational programs prescribed by the Board, or (iii) by rendering\r at any site any health care services within the limits of his license,\r voluntarily and without compensation, to any patient of any clinic which is\r organized in whole or in part for the delivery of health care services without\r charge as provided in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-106\">54.1-106</a>;</p>\r \r <p>17. The performance of the duties of any active duty health\r care provider in active service in the army, navy, coast guard, marine corps,\r air force, or public health service of the United States at any public or\r private health care facility while such individual is so commissioned or\r serving and in accordance with his official military duties;</p>\r \r <p>18. Any masseur, who publicly represents himself as such, from\r performing services within the scope of his usual professional activities and\r in conformance with state law;</p>\r \r <p>19. Any person from performing services in the lawful conduct\r of his particular profession or business under state law;</p>\r \r <p>20. Any person from rendering emergency care pursuant to the\r provisions of § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/8.01-225\">8.01-225</a>;</p>\r \r <p>21. Qualified emergency medical services personnel, when\r acting within the scope of their certification, and licensed health care\r practitioners, when acting within their scope of practice, from following\r Durable Do Not Resuscitate Orders issued in accordance with § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2987.1\">54.1-2987.1</a> and\r Board of Health regulations, or licensed health care practitioners from\r following any other written order of a physician not to resuscitate a patient\r in the event of cardiac or respiratory arrest;</p>\r \r <p>22. Any commissioned or contract medical officer of the army,\r navy, coast guard or air force rendering services voluntarily and without\r compensation while deemed to be licensed pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-106\">54.1-106</a>;</p>\r \r <p>23. Any<s> provider of a chemical dependency treatment program\r who is certified as an &quot;acupuncture detoxification specialist&quot; by the\r National Acupuncture Detoxification Association or an equivalent certifying\r body, from administering auricular acupuncture treatment under the appropriate\r supervision of a National Acupuncture Detoxification Association certified\r licensed physician or licensed acupuncturist</s><ins> person from engaging in the\r five needle auricular acupuncture protocol (5NP), a standardized five needle\r protocol wherein up to five needles are inserted into the external human ear to\r provide relief from the effects of behavioral health conditions, provided such\r person (i) has appropriate training in the 5NP, including training established\r by the National Acupuncture Detoxification Association or equivalent certifying\r body; (ii) does not use any letters, words, or insignia indicating or implying\r that the person is an acupuncturist; and (iii) makes no statements implying\r that his practice of the 5NP is licensed, certified, or otherwise overseen by\r the Commonwealth. Treatment utilizing the 5NP pursuant to this subdivision\r shall be strictly limited to the insertion of disposable sterile acupuncture\r needles into the ear and only in compliance with the 5NP. The application or\r insertion of needles anywhere else on the body of another person by a person\r acting under the provisions of this subdivision shall be considered engaging in\r the practice of acupuncture without a license</ins>;</p>\r \r <p>24. Any employee of any assisted living facility who is\r certified in cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR) acting in compliance with the\r patient\'s individualized service plan and with the written order of the\r attending physician not to resuscitate a patient in the event of cardiac or\r respiratory arrest;</p>\r \r <p>25. Any person working as a health assistant under the\r direction of a licensed medical or osteopathic doctor within the Department of\r Corrections, the Department of Juvenile Justice or local correctional\r facilities;</p>\r \r <p>26. Any employee of a school board, authorized by a prescriber\r and trained in the administration of insulin and glucagon, when, upon the\r authorization of a prescriber and the written request of the parents as defined\r in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/22.1-1\">22.1-1</a>, assisting with the administration of insulin or administrating\r glucagon to a student diagnosed as having diabetes and who requires insulin\r injections during the school day or for whom glucagon has been prescribed for\r the emergency treatment of hypoglycemia;</p>\r \r <p>27. Any practitioner of the healing arts or other profession\r regulated by the Board from rendering free health care to an underserved\r population of Virginia who (i) does not regularly practice his profession in\r Virginia, (ii) holds a current valid license or certificate to practice his\r profession in another state, territory, district or possession of the United\r States, (iii) volunteers to provide free health care to an underserved area of\r the Commonwealth under the auspices of a publicly supported all volunteer,\r nonprofit organization that sponsors the provision of health care to\r populations of underserved people, (iv) files a copy of the license or\r certification issued in such other jurisdiction with the Board, (v) notifies\r the Board at least five business days prior to the voluntary provision of\r services of the dates and location of such service, and (vi) acknowledges, in\r writing, that such licensure exemption shall only be valid, in compliance with\r the Board\'s regulations, during the limited period that such free health care\r is made available through the volunteer, nonprofit organization on the dates\r and at the location filed with the Board. The Board may deny the right to\r practice in Virginia to any practitioner of the healing arts whose license or\r certificate has been previously suspended or revoked, who has been convicted of\r a felony or who is otherwise found to be in violation of applicable laws or\r regulations. However, the Board shall allow a practitioner of the healing arts\r who meets the above criteria to provide volunteer services without prior notice\r for a period of up to three days, provided the nonprofit organization verifies\r that the practitioner has a valid, unrestricted license in another state;</p>\r \r <p>28. Any registered nurse, acting as an agent of the Department\r of Health, from obtaining specimens of sputum or other bodily fluid from\r persons in whom the diagnosis of active tuberculosis disease, as defined in §\r <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-49.1\">32.1-49.1</a>, is suspected and submitting orders for testing of such specimens to\r the Division of Consolidated Laboratories or other public health laboratories,\r designated by the State Health Commissioner, for the purpose of determining the\r presence or absence of tubercle bacilli as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-49.1\">32.1-49.1</a>;</p>\r \r <p>29. Any physician of medicine or osteopathy or advanced\r practice registered nurse from delegating to a registered nurse under his\r supervision the screening and testing of children for elevated blood-lead\r levels when such testing is conducted (i) in accordance with a written protocol\r between the physician or advanced practice registered nurse and the registered\r nurse and (ii) in compliance with the Board of Health\'s regulations promulgated\r pursuant to §§ <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-46.1\">32.1-46.1</a> and <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/32.1-46.2\">32.1-46.2</a>. Any follow-up testing or treatment\r shall be conducted at the direction of a physician or an advanced practice\r registered nurse;</p>\r \r <p>30. Any practitioner of one of the professions regulated by\r the Board of Medicine who is in good standing with the applicable regulatory\r agency in another state or Canada from engaging in the practice of that\r profession when the practitioner is in Virginia temporarily with an\r out-of-state athletic team or athlete for the duration of the athletic\r tournament, game, or event in which the team or athlete is competing;</p>\r \r <p>31. Any person from performing state or federally funded\r health care tasks directed by the consumer, which are typically self-performed,\r for an individual who lives in a private residence and who, by reason of\r disability, is unable to perform such tasks but who is capable of directing the\r appropriate performance of such tasks;</p>\r \r <p>32. Any practitioner of one of the professions regulated by\r the Board of Medicine who is in good standing with the applicable regulatory\r agency in another state from engaging in the practice of that profession in\r Virginia with a patient who is being transported to or from a Virginia hospital\r for care;</p>\r \r <p>33. Any doctor of medicine or osteopathy, physician assistant,\r or advanced practice registered nurse who would otherwise be subject to\r licensure by the Board who holds an active, unrestricted license in another\r state, the District of Columbia, or a United States territory or possession and\r who is in good standing with the applicable regulatory agency in that state,\r the District of Columbia, or that United States territory or possession who\r provides behavioral health services, as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/37.2-100\">37.2-100</a>, from engaging in\r the practice of his profession and providing behavioral health services to a\r patient located in the Commonwealth in accordance with the standard of care\r when (i) such practice is for the purpose of providing continuity of care through\r the use of telemedicine services as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/38.2-3418.16\">38.2-3418.16</a> and (ii) the\r practitioner has previously established a practitioner-patient relationship\r with the patient and has performed an in-person evaluation of the patient\r within the previous year. A practitioner who provides behavioral health\r services to a patient located in the Commonwealth through use of telemedicine\r services pursuant to this subdivision may provide such services for a period of\r no more than one year from the date on which the practitioner began providing\r such services to such patient;</p>\r \r <p>34. Any employee of a program licensed by the Department of\r Behavioral Health and Developmental Services who is certified in\r cardiopulmonary resuscitation from acting in compliance with a program participant\'s\r valid written order not to resuscitate issued in accordance with § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/54.1-2987.1\">54.1-2987.1</a>\r if such valid written order not to resuscitate is included in the program\r participant\'s individualized service plan; or</p>\r \r <p>35. Any doctor of medicine or osteopathy, physician assistant,\r respiratory therapist, occupational therapist, or advanced practice registered\r nurse who would otherwise be subject to licensure by the Board who holds an\r active, unrestricted license in another state or the District of Columbia and\r who is in good standing with the applicable regulatory agency in that state or\r the District of Columbia from engaging in the practice of that profession in\r the Commonwealth with a patient located in the Commonwealth when (i) such\r practice is for the purpose of providing continuity of care through the use of\r telemedicine services as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/38.2-3418.16\">38.2-3418.16</a> and (ii) the patient is a\r current patient of the practitioner with whom the practitioner has previously\r established a practitioner-patient relationship and the practitioner has\r performed an in-person examination of the patient within the previous 12\r months. </p>\r \r <p>For purposes of this subdivision, if such practitioner with\r whom the patient has previously established a practitioner-patient relationship\r is unavailable at the time in which the patient seeks continuity of care,\r another practitioner of the same subspecialty at the same practice group with\r access to the patient\'s treatment history may provide continuity of care using\r telemedicine services until the practitioner with whom the patient has a\r previously established practitioner-patient relationship becomes available. For\r the purposes of this subdivision, &quot;practitioner of the same\r subspecialty&quot; means a practitioner who utilizes the same subspecialty taxonomy\r code designation for claims processing. </p>\r \r <p>For the purposes of this subdivision, if a patient is (a) an\r enrollee of a health maintenance organization that contracts with a\r multispecialty group of practitioners, each of whom is licensed by the Board of\r Medicine, and (b) a current patient of at least one practitioner who is a\r member of the multispecialty group with whom such practitioner has previously\r established a practitioner-patient relationship and of whom such practitioner\r has performed an in-person examination within the previous 12 months, the\r patient shall be deemed to be a current patient of each practitioner in the\r multispecialty group with whom each such practitioner has established a\r practitioner-patient relationship.</p>\r \r <p>B. Notwithstanding any provision of law or regulation to the\r contrary, military medical personnel, as defined in § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/2.2-2001.4\">2.2-2001.4</a>, while\r participating in a program established by the Department of Veterans Services\r pursuant to § <a href=\"http://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/2.2-2001.4\">2.2-2001.4</a>, may practice under the supervision of a licensed\r physician or podiatrist or the chief medical officer of an organization\r participating in such program, or his designee who is a licensee of the Board\r and supervising within his scope of practice.</p>',NULL,0,'2024-02-06 21:55:02','2025-11-06 00:15:32');
