(35,78269,31,'The bill establishing the right to obtain contraception was initially passed by the Senate with a narrow vote of 21-18 and later passed by the House with a substitute by a vote of 54-41. After both chambers agreed on the House\'s substitute, the bill was enrolled and sent to the governor, who proposed amendments. The Senate rejected the governor\'s recommendations, and the bill was communicated back to the governor for final action.','y','2026-01-09 11:01:58','2026-01-09 11:01:58');
