(42,76706,31,'The bill proposing a constitutional amendment to establish a fundamental right to reproductive freedom was initially continued to 2025 by the House Privileges and Elections Committee. It was later reported with a substitute and narrowly passed the House with a 51-48 vote. The Senate also agreed to the bill with a 21-18 vote, and it was subsequently enrolled, signed by legislative leaders, and assigned as Chapter 600, set to take effect on July 1, 2025.','y','2026-01-09 12:01:57','2026-01-09 12:01:57');
