INSERT INTO `comments` VALUES
(16179,90506,74670,'Anonymous','example@example.com',NULL,'127.192.35.27','This is an endangerment to all patients everywhere. CNRAs do not have the training of expertise to practice independently.','comment','published','n','2024-02-05 02:27:37','2024-02-05 02:27:37'),
(16184,90510,74670,'Liam','example@example.com',NULL,'127.26.62.119','I strongly advice against CRNAs practicing independently. \n\nThis could lead to the endangerment of patients. \nCRNAs have 2,000 clinical hours while anesthesiologists have between 12,000-16,000 hours. \nCRNAs are trained to work with anesthesiologists, which is why they have significantly less experience. \n\nOverall, passing this bill could lead to the suffering of innocent people.','comment','published','n','2024-02-05 17:10:00','2024-02-05 17:10:00'),
(16187,90515,74670,'Anon','example@example.com',NULL,'127.5.10.35','I fully support the independent practice of CRNA\'s. There is a lot of fear mongering regarding CRNA independent practice.\nCRNA\'s are the ones administering the anesthesia the entire time. We read the same books as physician anesthesiologists do for anesthesia. It\'s all about market control.','comment','published','n','2024-02-06 02:33:14','2024-02-06 02:33:14'),
(16202,90546,74670,'Evan','example@example.com',NULL,'127.145.177.233','This extremely dangerous legislation. CRNAs have nowhere near the education, training, and experience of board certified anesthesiologist. A US M.D undergoes 4 years of rigorous academic and clinical education as well as 3 brutal step exams simply to enter residency. They then practice their specialty across multiple practice domains included very high-risk settings so they can learn the ins an outs of their speciality. Even a Family Medicine resident going into primary care clinic will learn how to manage patients in the Intensive Care Unit. CRNAs recieve nowhere near this type of training and their training and education is hardly are regulated and standardized as M.Ds and D.Os. The only reason why people are even entertaining the idea of independent midlevel practice is because they have never had to see the results of unsupervised midlevel practice. \n\nThis legislation is designed entirely to undermine quality healthcare. It will allow massive healthcare systems to hire cheaper CRNAs and, because of their size, they will inevitably still profit even with the increased payouts owed for preventable medical mishaps. If this legislation passes in 10 years it will be hard to find a job as an Anesthesiologist in VA because the market will be saturated with lesser trained and lesser qualified CRNAs. \n\nYou, or someone you love, will all likely end up on an operating table one day. Anesthesia is serious business and a major source of mistakes in the healthcare setting. Do you really want to go under with an unsupervised CRNA brought in as a cost-cutting measure so that a University hospital could maximize its profits?','comment','published','n','2024-02-08 21:07:27','2024-02-08 21:07:27');
