INSERT INTO `comments` VALUES
(16112,90320,73286,'Bill Peabody','example@example.com',NULL,'127.46.0.51','Won\'t  many arrest subjects claim they were having a psychotic event?\nHard to prove.','comment','published','n','2024-01-21 19:12:29','2024-01-21 19:12:29'),
(16115,5059,73286,'Waldo Jaquith','example@example.com','https://waldo.jaquith.org/','127.31.162.105','The only reason police would be responding in this scenario is because of the mental health crisis—there would be no underlying crime requiring a police response.','comment','published','n','2024-01-21 19:54:21','2024-01-21 19:54:21'),
(16176,90477,73286,'Danielle Newman','example@example.com',NULL,'127.196.151.163','An individual having a true mental health crisis is easy to prove. It\'s the lack of empathy that causes confusion. Individuals in a mental health crisis should be handled with respect and understanding instead of violence and apathy. Police officers have a duty to de-escalate and establish safety protocol. I believe police officers need more specialized training on interacting with people dealing with a mental health crisis. Also, I would love to see Virginia hire social workers to work alongside officers when responding to mental health crisis calls.','comment','published','n','2024-02-03 00:34:27','2024-02-03 00:34:27');
